{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01H7rtf1HSE9XLmNSig6w8wg","type":"tool_result","content":"849\t**Before you stop:**\n850\t\n851\t- [ ] `node tools/test.mjs` is all green, with the hub suite passing all three runs.\n852\t- [ ] The scripted playthrough finishes the career with no Dev tools.\n853\t- [ ] The built HTML runs from `file://`, with `session.js` unmodified and first in `<head>`, and `pixel-engine.js` unedited in `src/`.\n854\t- [ ] Music starts at 10% on a fresh profile and in a session.\n855\t- [ ] Grep for `TODO`, `FIXME`, `placeholder`, `stub`, `coming soon`: nothing in the game.\n856\t- [ ] Every menu item does something. Every car, track, test and event is reachable.\n857\t- [ ] You looked at the 1080p screenshots.\n858\t- [ ] About/Credits shows real answers. The exit-interview file parses as JSON. Your chat reply carries the same information.\n859\t- [ ] No stray servers or browsers of yours left running.\n860\t\n861\t---\n862\t\n863\t## Appendix A: `src/game/sim/sim.js`\n864\t\n865\tTested code. It ran every car on every track, an 8-car race with contact, and the checks in Appendix B. Port it as is, then extend it.\n866\t\n867\t**How the pieces connect:**\n868\t\n869\t- Per fixed step (60 Hz), get one input per car, then 4 times: `stepCar` for each car, `collideCars(field)` when contact is on.\n870\t- `env` is optional per step: `gripScale`, `powerScale`, `brakeScale`, `aeroScale`, `wearRate`, `fuelRate`, `wallLoss`, `kerb`. Dev mode's sliders write here.\n871\t- Car-level fields the race code sets: `c.dragScale` (slipstream), `c.oil` (service), `c.inPit` (pit lane surface).\n872\t- `tr.wallL`, `tr.wallR` are per-sample barrier distances from the road edge. `tr.muScale` is rain. `tr.cornerS[n]` is corner n's apex.\n873\t- Everything is deterministic for the same inputs.\n874\t- Add reverse by setting `inp.reverse`. Add AI lapses and pit autopilot in `race.js`, not here.\n875\t\n876\t```js\n877\t// src/game/sim/sim.js: the race simulation. Pure JS, no engine, no DOM. Metres, seconds, kg, newtons, radians. Y up.\n878\t// Heading yaw: 0 faces +Z; forward = (sin yaw, cos yaw); the driver's right = (-cos yaw, sin yaw). Steer > 0 turns right.\n879\texport const G = 9.81, RHO = 1.2;\n880\texport const SURFACES = { // mu multiplies the tyre; drag is rolling drag in g at speed; tyre tables below may override mu\n881\t  asphalt: { mu: 1, drag: 0 }, kerb: { mu: 0.94, drag: 0.004 }, grass: { mu: 0.5, drag: 0.09 }, gravel: { mu: 0.55, drag: 0.16 },\n882\t  dirt: { mu: 0.62, drag: 0.02 }, apron: { mu: 0.9, drag: 0.004 },\n883\t};\n884\t\n885\t// ---------- Track: a closed polygon with rounded corners, [x, z, radius, y, width, bankDeg] per corner ----------\n886\texport function buildTrack(def, step = 4) {\n887\t  const C = def.corners, n = C.length, px = [], pz = [], key = [];\n888\t  const T0 = C.map((c, i) => {\n889\t    const a = C[(i - 1 + n) % n], b = C[(i + 1) % n];\n890\t    let ux = a[0] - c[0], uz = a[1] - c[1], vx = b[0] - c[0], vz = b[1] - c[1]; const ul = Math.hypot(ux, uz), vl = Math.hypot(vx, vz); ux /= ul; uz /= ul; vx /= vl; vz /= vl;\n891\t    const ang = Math.acos(Math.max(-1, Math.min(1, ux * vx + uz * vz))), t = c[2] / Math.tan(ang / 2), bx = ux + vx, bz = uz + vz, bl = Math.hypot(bx, bz), d = c[2] / Math.sin(ang / 2);\n892\t    return { inX: c[0] + ux * t, inZ: c[1] + uz * t, outX: c[0] + vx * t, outZ: c[1] + vz * t, cx: c[0] + (bx / bl) * d, cz: c[1] + (bz / bl) * d, r: c[2] };\n893\t  });\n894\t  const push = (x, z, k) => { px.push(x); pz.push(z); key.push(k); };\n895\t  const line = (x0, z0, x1, z1, ci, f0, f1) => { const m = Math.max(1, Math.round(Math.hypot(x1 - x0, z1 - z0))); for (let i = 0; i < m; i++) { const f = i / m; push(x0 + (x1 - x0) * f, z0 + (z1 - z0) * f, ci + f0 + (f1 - f0) * f); } };\n896\t  const midX = (C[n - 1][0] + C[0][0]) / 2, midZ = (C[n - 1][1] + C[0][1]) / 2; let cx = midX, cz = midZ; // s = 0 is the middle of the last edge\n897\t  for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n898\t    const t = T0[i]; line(cx, cz, t.inX, t.inZ, i - 1, i === 0 ? 0.5 : 0, 0.85);\n899\t    const a0 = Math.atan2(t.inZ - t.cz, t.inX - t.cx); let da = Math.atan2(t.outZ - t.cz, t.outX - t.cx) - a0; while (da > Math.PI) da -= 2 * Math.PI; while (da < -Math.PI) da += 2 * Math.PI;\n900\t    const m = Math.max(1, Math.round(Math.abs(da) * t.r)); for (let k = 0; k < m; k++) { const f = k / m, a = a0 + da * f; push(t.cx + t.r * Math.cos(a), t.cz + t.r * Math.sin(a), i - 1 + 0.85 + 0.15 * f); }\n901\t    cx = t.outX; cz = t.outZ;\n902\t  }\n903\t  line(cx, cz, midX, midZ, n - 1, 0, 0.5);\n904\t  const m = px.length, smooth = (a, r) => { const o = new Float64Array(m); let s = 0; for (let i = -r; i <= r; i++) s += a[(i + m) % m]; for (let i = 0; i < m; i++) { o[i] = s / (2 * r + 1); s += a[(i + r + 1) % m] - a[(i - r + m) % m]; } return o; };\n905\t  const sx = smooth(smooth(px, 7), 7), sz = smooth(smooth(pz, 7), 7), cum = new Float64Array(m + 1);\n906\t  for (let i = 0; i < m; i++) cum[i + 1] = cum[i] + Math.hypot(sx[(i + 1) % m] - sx[i], sz[(i + 1) % m] - sz[i]);\n907\t  const length = cum[m], N = Math.round(length / step), ds = length / N, A = () => new Float64Array(N);\n908\t  const tr = { def, N, ds, length, x: A(), z: A(), y: A(), width: A(), bank: A(), tx: A(), tz: A(), kappa: A(), slope: A(), wallL: A().fill(def.runoff ?? 9), wallR: A().fill(def.runoff ?? 9), cornerS: new Array(n).fill(0), surface: def.surface ?? 'asphalt', edge: def.edge ?? 'grass', muScale: 1 };\n909\t  const ease = (f) => f * f * (3 - 2 * f), attr = (k, q) => { const ci = Math.floor(k), f = ease(k - ci), a = C[(ci + n) % n], b = C[(ci + 1 + n) % n]; return a[q] + (b[q] - a[q]) * f; };\n910\t  for (let i = 0, j = 0; i < N; i++) {\n911\t    const s = i * ds; while (cum[j + 1] < s) j++;\n912\t    const f = (s - cum[j]) / (cum[j + 1] - cum[j]), q = (j + 1) % m, k = key[j];\n913\t    tr.x[i] = sx[j] + (sx[q] - sx[j]) * f; tr.z[i] = sz[j] + (sz[q] - sz[j]) * f; tr.y[i] = attr(k, 3); tr.width[i] = attr(k, 4); tr.bank[i] = (attr(k, 5) * Math.PI) / 180;\n914\t  }\n915\t  for (let j = 0, ci = 0; j < m && ci < n; j++) if (key[j] >= ci - 1 + 0.925) tr.cornerS[ci++] = cum[j]; // s at each corner's apex\n916\t  for (const [cs, cl, ch] of def.crests ?? []) for (let i = 0; i < N; i++) { const d = (i * ds - cs) / cl; if (Math.abs(d) < 1) tr.y[i] += ch * (0.5 + 0.5 * Math.cos(Math.PI * d)); }\n917\t  for (let i = 0; i < N; i++) { const p = (i - 1 + N) % N, q = (i + 1) % N, dx = tr.x[q] - tr.x[p], dz = tr.z[q] - tr.z[p], l = Math.hypot(dx, dz); tr.tx[i] = dx / l; tr.tz[i] = dz / l; tr.slope[i] = (tr.y[q] - tr.y[p]) / l; }\n918\t  for (let i = 0; i < N; i++) { const p = (i - 1 + N) % N, q = (i + 1) % N; tr.kappa[i] = (tr.tx[p] * tr.tz[q] - tr.tz[p] * tr.tx[q]) / (2 * ds); tr.bank[i] *= Math.sign(tr.kappa[i] || 1); } // kappa > 0 turns right; bank > 0 pushes right\n919\t  return tr;\n920\t}\n921\t// t > 0 is the driver's right of the centreline: right = (-tz, tx). Search near the last index, so crossings can't confuse it.\n922\texport function locate(tr, px, pz, hint, out) {\n923\t  let best = hint, bd = Infinity;\n924\t  for (let k = -12; k <= 12; k++) { const i = (hint + k + tr.N) % tr.N, d = (px - tr.x[i]) ** 2 + (pz - tr.z[i]) ** 2; if (d < bd) { bd = d; best = i; } }\n925\t  const dx = px - tr.x[best], dz = pz - tr.z[best];\n926\t  out.i = best; out.s = (best * tr.ds + dx * tr.tx[best] + dz * tr.tz[best] + tr.length) % tr.length; out.t = -dx * tr.tz[best] + dz * tr.tx[best];\n927\t}\n928\texport function racingLine(tr, margin = 1.6, iters = 1500) { // elastic band: each point relaxes to its neighbours' midpoint, inside the track\n929\t  const off = new Float64Array(tr.N), px = Float64Array.from(tr.x), pz = Float64Array.from(tr.z), kappa = new Float64Array(tr.N), N = tr.N;\n930\t  for (let it = 0; it < iters; it++) for (let i = 0; i < N; i++) {\n931\t    const p = (i - 1 + N) % N, q = (i + 1) % N, dx = (px[p] + px[q]) / 2 - tr.x[i], dz = (pz[p] + pz[q]) / 2 - tr.z[i], lim = tr.width[i] / 2 - margin;\n932\t    off[i] = Math.max(-lim, Math.min(lim, -dx * tr.tz[i] + dz * tr.tx[i])); px[i] = tr.x[i] - off[i] * tr.tz[i]; pz[i] = tr.z[i] + off[i] * tr.tx[i];\n933\t  }\n934\t  for (let i = 0; i < N; i++) { const a = (i - 3 + N) % N, c = (i + 3) % N, ax = px[i] - px[a], az = pz[i] - pz[a], bx = px[c] - px[i], bz = pz[c] - pz[i], la = Math.hypot(ax, az), lb = Math.hypot(bx, bz); kappa[i] = (2 * (ax * bz - az * bx)) / (la * lb * (la + lb)); }\n935\t  return { off, px, pz, kappa };\n936\t}\n937\texport function speedProfile(tr, line, c, surfMu = 1) { // the fastest the car can follow the line, friction circle included\n938\t  const N = tr.N, v = new Float64Array(N), ds = tr.ds, m = c.mass, muEff = c.tyreMu * (c.clA > 0.5 ? 0.76 : 0.86) * surfMu, down = (RHO * c.clA) / (2 * m), dragK = (0.5 * RHO * c.cdA) / m;\n939\t  const grip = (sp) => muEff * (G + down * sp * sp);\n940\t  for (let i = 0; i < N; i++) {\n941\t    const k = Math.max(Math.abs(line.kappa[i]), 1e-5), tb = Math.tan(Math.abs(tr.bank[i])) * (Math.sign(tr.bank[i]) === Math.sign(line.kappa[i]) ? 1 : -1), muB = (muEff + tb) / Math.max(0.2, 1 - muEff * tb), den = k - muB * down;\n942\t    v[i] = Math.min(den > 1e-5 ? Math.sqrt((muB * G) / den) : 110, c.vMax ?? 110);\n943\t  }\n944\t  const left = (sp, i) => { const A = grip(sp), lat = sp * sp * Math.abs(line.kappa[i]); return Math.sqrt(Math.max(0.0025 * A * A, A * A - lat * lat)); };\n945\t  for (let pass = 0; pass < 2; pass++) {\n946\t    for (let i = N - 1; i >= 0; i--) { const j = (i + 1) % N, a = left(v[j], j) * 0.82 + dragK * v[j] * v[j]; v[i] = Math.min(v[i], Math.sqrt(v[j] * v[j] + 2 * a * ds)); }\n947\t    for (let i = 0; i < N; i++) { const j = (i + 1) % N, a = Math.min(left(v[i], i), (c.powerW * 0.85) / (m * Math.max(v[i], 8))) - dragK * v[i] * v[i]; v[j] = Math.min(v[j], Math.sqrt(Math.max(v[i] * v[i] + 2 * a * ds, 1))); }\n948\t  }\n949\t  return v;\n950\t}\n951\t\n952\t// ---------- Car ----------\n953\texport function torqueShape(x, d) { // torque against rpm / rpmPeak; peak power lands at x = 1\n954\t  const low = d.turbo ? 0.5 : 0.62, rise = Math.min(1, low + (1 - low) * Math.min(1, x / 0.7)), fall = x <= 1 ? 1 - 0.14 * Math.max(0, (x - 0.7) / 0.3) : 0.86 - 0.9 * (x - 1);\n955\t  return Math.max(0.05, rise * fall);\n956\t}\n957\texport function carParams(d) { // d: a row of the car table after tuning\n958\t  const L = d.wheelbase, powerW = d.powerPS * 735.5, omega = (d.rpmPeak * 2 * Math.PI) / 60;\n959\t  return { ...d, mass: d.massKg, L, a: L * (1 - d.frontWeight), b: L * d.frontWeight, T: d.track ?? 1.5, h: d.cgH ?? 0.5, R: d.wheelR ?? 0.31, Izz: d.massKg * (0.25 * L * L + 0.35), powerW, Tpeak: powerW / (omega * torqueShape(1, d)), tyreMu: d.tyreMu ?? 1, alphaP: d.alphaP ?? 0.125, clA: d.clA ?? 0.1, cdA: d.cdA ?? 0.7, aeroF: d.aeroF ?? 0.45, rollF: d.rollF ?? 0.56, loadK: d.loadK ?? 0.1, lsd: d.lsd ?? 0, brakeF: d.brakeF ?? 0.62, brakeG: d.brakeG ?? 1.25, rearStiff: d.rearStiff ?? 1.3, lock: d.lock ?? 0.6, shiftTime: d.shiftTime ?? 0.16, idle: d.idle ?? 900, launch: d.launch ?? 3200, awdFront: d.awdFront ?? 0.4, engineBrake: d.engineBrake ?? 0.16 };\n960\t}\n961\texport function newCar(p, tr, i = 0, t = 0) {\n962\t  const rx = -tr.tz[i], rz = tr.tx[i], y = tr.y[i];\n963\t  return { p, x: tr.x[i] + rx * t, z: tr.z[i] + rz * t, y, vy: 0, yaw: Math.atan2(tr.tx[i], tr.tz[i]), vx: 0, vz: 0, r: 0, delta: 0, ax: 0, ay: 0, gear: 1, shift: 0, rpm: p.idle, spool: 0, fz: [0, 0, 0, 0], fy: [0, 0, 0, 0], use: [0, 0, 0, 0], loc: { i, s: i * tr.ds, t }, u: 0, w: 0, beta: 0, sliding: false, spinning: false, locked: false, airborne: false, onTrack: true, surface: tr.surface, wear: [1, 1, 1, 1], fuel: 1, wallHits: 0, contact: 0, rev: 0 };\n964\t}\n965\tconst curve = (x) => { const a = Math.abs(x), v = a < 1 ? Math.sin((a * Math.PI) / 2) : Math.max(0.86, 1 - 0.07 * (a - 1)); return x < 0 ? -v : v; };\n966\tconst XF = (p) => [p.a, p.a, -p.b, -p.b], XR = (p) => [-p.T / 2, p.T / 2, -p.T / 2, p.T / 2];\n967\t// One substep (4 per fixedUpdate). inp: { steer -1..1, throttle, brake, handbrake, abs, tcs 0..1, asm 0..1, auto, up, down, steerRate }\n968\texport function stepCar(c, inp, dt, tr, env = {}) {\n969\t  const p = c.p, sn = Math.sin(c.yaw), cs = Math.cos(c.yaw), u = c.vx * sn + c.vz * cs, w = -c.vx * cs + c.vz * sn;\n970\t  c.u = u; c.w = w; locate(tr, c.x, c.z, c.loc.i, c.loc);\n971\t  const i0 = c.loc.i, halfW = tr.width[i0] / 2, off = Math.abs(c.loc.t) - halfW, kerbW = env.kerb ?? 1.6;\n972\t  const sName = c.inPit ? 'apron' : off < -0.1 ? tr.surface : off < kerbW && tr.surface === 'asphalt' ? 'kerb' : tr.edge, surf = SURFACES[sName];\n973\t  c.surface = sName; c.onTrack = off < kerbW;\n974\t  const tyreOnSurf = (p.tyreTable?.[sName] ?? surf.mu) * (env.gripScale ?? 1) * (tr.muScale ?? 1);\n975\t\n976\t  // Heave: a sprung mass over the surface, so crests lighten the car and jumps leave the ground.\n977\t  const bk = tr.bank[i0], gy = tr.y[i0] + tr.slope[i0] * (c.loc.s - i0 * tr.ds) - c.loc.t * Math.sin(bk);\n978\t  const gyRate = tr.slope[i0] * u, pen = gy - c.y, wn = Math.sqrt(G / 0.08), Fs = pen > -0.02 ? Math.max(0, p.mass * G * (1 + pen / 0.08) + 2 * 0.5 * p.mass * wn * (gyRate - c.vy)) : 0;\n979\t  c.vy += (Fs / p.mass - G) * dt; c.y += c.vy * dt; if (c.y < gy - 0.25) { c.y = gy - 0.25; c.vy = Math.max(c.vy, gyRate); }\n980\t  const heave = Fs / (p.mass * G); c.airborne = Fs <= 0;\n981\t\n982\t  // Steering stops near the front tyres' peak at this speed and opens with body slip, so counter-steer is always there.\n983\t  const au = Math.max(Math.abs(u), 5), beta = Math.abs(u) > 3 ? Math.atan2(w, Math.abs(u)) : 0; c.beta = beta;\n984\t  const limit = Math.min(p.lock, Math.atan((p.L * p.tyreMu * G * 1.1) / (au * au)) + p.alphaP * 0.9 + Math.abs(beta));\n985\t  const rate = (inp.steerRate ?? 3) * dt; c.delta += Math.max(-rate, Math.min(rate, inp.steer * limit - c.delta));\n986\t  const sd = Math.sin(c.delta), cd = Math.cos(c.delta);\n987\t\n988\t  // Loads: static, aero, heave, banking, then longitudinal and lateral transfer.\n989\t  const aero = 0.5 * RHO * p.clA * (env.aeroScale ?? 1) * u * u, bankLoad = Math.cos(bk) + Math.max(0, (u * u * tr.kappa[i0] * Math.sin(bk)) / G), fw = p.b / p.L;\n990\t  const sF = (p.mass * G * bankLoad * heave * fw) / 2 + (aero * p.aeroF) / 2, sR = (p.mass * G * bankLoad * heave * (1 - fw)) / 2 + (aero * (1 - p.aeroF)) / 2;\n991\t  const dLong = (p.mass * c.ax * p.h) / p.L / 2, dLatF = (p.mass * c.ay * p.h * p.rollF) / p.T, dLatR = (p.mass * c.ay * p.h * (1 - p.rollF)) / p.T, fz = c.fz; // +ay pushes right: load moves to the left wheels\n992\t  fz[0] = Math.max(0, sF - dLong + dLatF); fz[1] = Math.max(0, sF - dLong - dLatF); fz[2] = Math.max(0, sR + dLong + dLatR); fz[3] = Math.max(0, sR + dLong - dLatR);\n993\t  const Fz0 = (p.mass * G) / 4, Fmax = [0, 0, 0, 0], sL = [sF, sF, sR, sR];\n994\t  for (let i = 0; i < 4; i++) Fmax[i] = fz[i] * p.tyreMu * tyreOnSurf * (0.72 + 0.28 * Math.sqrt(Math.max(0, c.wear[i]))) * Math.max(0.82, Math.min(1.08, 1 - p.loadK * (fz[i] / Fz0 - 1)));\n995\t\n996\t  // Gearbox and engine. rpm follows the road, the clutch slips below launch speed.\n997\t  const gears = p.gears, Gk = gears[c.gear - 1] * p.final, wheelRpm = (Math.abs(u) / p.R) * (60 / (2 * Math.PI));\n998\t  let rpm = wheelRpm * Gk; const clutchRpm = p.idle + p.launch * inp.throttle; if (rpm < clutchRpm) rpm = clutchRpm;\n999\t  if (c.shift > 0) c.shift -= dt;\n1000\t  if (c.shift <= 0) {\n1001\t    if (inp.auto !== false) {\n1002\t      if (rpm > p.upshift && c.gear < gears.length && inp.throttle > 0.1) { c.gear++; c.shift = p.shiftTime; }\n1003\t      else if (c.gear > 1) { const down = wheelRpm * gears[c.gear - 2] * p.final; if (down < p.upshift * 0.8 && (inp.throttle < 0.2 || down < p.rpmPeak * 0.8)) { c.gear--; c.shift = p.shiftTime * 0.6; } }\n1004\t    } else {\n1005\t      if (inp.up && c.gear < gears.length) { c.gear++; c.shift = p.shiftTime; }\n1006\t      if (inp.down && c.gear > 1 && wheelRpm * gears[c.gear - 2] * p.final < p.redline) { c.gear--; c.shift = p.shiftTime * 0.6; }\n1007\t    }\n1008\t  }\n1009\t  c.rpm = Math.min(rpm, p.redline + 200);\n1010\t  const x = rpm / p.rpmPeak, throttle = rpm >= p.redline || c.fuel <= 0 ? 0 : inp.throttle;\n1011\t  if (p.turbo) c.spool += ((throttle > 0.5 && rpm > p.rpmPeak * 0.4 ? 1 : 0.15) - c.spool) * Math.min(1, dt / (p.turboLag ?? 0.6));\n1012\t  const boost = p.turbo ? 0.55 + 0.45 * c.spool : 1, Te = throttle * p.Tpeak * torqueShape(x, p) * boost * (env.powerScale ?? 1) * (c.oil ?? 1), eb = (1 - throttle) * p.engineBrake * p.Tpeak * Math.min(1, x);\n1013\t  let drive = c.shift > 0 || inp.handbrake ? 0 : ((Te - eb) * Gk * 0.9) / p.R; if (inp.reverse) drive = -Math.min(3500, Math.abs(drive));\n1014\t  c.fuel = Math.max(0, c.fuel - throttle * (rpm / p.redline) * dt * (env.fuelRate ?? 0.0018));\n1015\t  const split = p.layout === '4WD' ? p.awdFront : p.layout === 'FF' ? 1 : 0;\n1016\t\n1017\t  // Traction control trims drive to what the driven tyres have left after cornering.\n1018\t  const free = (i) => Math.sqrt(Math.max(0.04 * Fmax[i] * Fmax[i], Fmax[i] * Fmax[i] - c.fy[i] * c.fy[i])), cap = (l, r) => 2 * Math.min(l, r) + p.lsd * Math.abs(l - r);\n1019\t  if (inp.tcs > 0 && drive > 0) { const fA = cap(free(0), free(1)), rA = cap(free(2), free(3)), allow = (split === 1 ? fA : split === 0 ? rA : Math.min(fA / split, rA / (1 - split))) * (1.05 - 0.35 * inp.tcs); drive = Math.min(drive, allow); }\n1020\t  const axle = (F, l, r) => { // the differential: open splits evenly and is held back by the lighter wheel; lsd lends it the other wheel's grip\n1021\t    const mag = Math.abs(F), sign = Math.sign(F), low = Math.min(l, r), top = cap(l, r); let a = mag / 2, b = mag / 2, spin = false;\n1022\t    if (mag > top) { spin = true; a = l <= r ? low : top - low; b = l <= r ? top - low : low; } else if (mag / 2 > low) { a = l <= r ? low : mag - low; b = l <= r ? mag - low : low; }\n1023\t    return [a * sign, b * sign, spin];\n1024\t  };\n1025\t  const [d0, d1, s0] = axle(drive * split, Fmax[0], Fmax[1]), [d2, d3, s1] = axle(drive * (1 - split), Fmax[2], Fmax[3]), fxD = [d0, d1, d2, d3]; c.spinning = s0 || s1;\n1026\t\n1027\t  // Tyres: lateral force from slip angle, longitudinal from drive and brake, both inside the friction circle.\n1028\t  const Bmax = p.brakeG * p.mass * G * (env.brakeScale ?? 1), xf = XF(p), xr = XR(p), tanP = Math.tan(p.alphaP); let Ff = 0, Fr = 0, M = 0; c.sliding = false; c.locked = false;\n1029\t  for (let i = 0; i < 4; i++) {\n1030\t    const isF = i < 2, vf = u - c.r * xr[i], vr = w + c.r * xf[i], vLong = isF ? vf * cd + vr * sd : vf, vLat = isF ? -vf * sd + vr * cd : vr, lim = Math.max(1, Fmax[i]), dir = Math.abs(vLong) < 0.3 ? 0 : Math.sign(vLong);\n1031\t    let Fx = fxD[i], locked = false, bd = inp.brake * Bmax * (isF ? p.brakeF : 1 - p.brakeF) * 0.5; const hb = !isF && inp.handbrake; if (hb) bd = 1e9;\n1032\t    if (bd > 0) { if (inp.abs !== false && !hb) bd = Math.min(bd, Math.sqrt(Math.max(0.04 * lim * lim, lim * lim - c.fy[i] * c.fy[i])) * 0.9); else if (bd > lim) { bd = lim * 0.82; locked = true; c.locked = true; } Fx -= bd * dir; }\n1033\t    let rho = Math.abs(Fx) / lim, latCap; if (locked) latCap = 0.28; else if (rho > 1) { Fx = Math.sign(Fx) * lim * 0.95; latCap = 0.3; rho = 1; } else latCap = Math.max(0.3, Math.sqrt(1 - rho * rho));\n1034\t    const tanA = vLat / Math.max(Math.abs(vLong), 3.5), peak = tanP * Math.max(0.35, Math.pow(fz[i] / Math.max(1, sL[i]), 0.8)) * (isF ? 1 : 1 / p.rearStiff), Fy = -lim * latCap * curve(tanA / peak);\n1035\t    c.fy[i] = Fy; c.use[i] = Math.abs(tanA / peak); if (Math.abs(tanA) > peak * 1.3 && Math.abs(u) > 4) c.sliding = true;\n1036\t    c.wear[i] = Math.max(0, c.wear[i] - dt * (env.wearRate ?? 0.0012) * (p.wearX ?? 1) * (0.15 + c.use[i] * c.use[i] + rho * rho));\n1037\t    const bFf = isF ? Fx * cd - Fy * sd : Fx, bFr = isF ? Fx * sd + Fy * cd : Fy; Ff += bFf; Fr += bFr; M += xf[i] * bFr - xr[i] * bFf;\n1038\t  }\n1039\t  // Drag, surface, grade, banking; ASM adds a moment against yaw that grip doesn't explain.\n1040\t  const drag = 0.5 * RHO * p.cdA * (c.dragScale ?? 1) * u * Math.abs(u), sd2 = Math.sign(u); Ff -= drag + 0.012 * p.mass * G * sd2 + surf.drag * Math.min(1, Math.abs(u) / 15) * p.mass * G * sd2 + p.mass * G * tr.slope[i0]; Fr += p.mass * G * Math.sin(bk);\n1041\t  if (inp.asm > 0 && Math.abs(u) > 6) { const excess = c.r - Fr / p.mass / Math.max(Math.abs(u), 6), lim = inp.asm * p.mass * 6; M += Math.max(-lim, Math.min(lim, -excess * inp.asm * p.Izz * 9)); }\n1042\t  const f = Math.min(1, dt / 0.05); c.ax += (Ff / p.mass - c.ax) * f; c.ay += (Fr / p.mass - c.ay) * f;\n1043\t  c.vx += ((Ff * sn - Fr * cs) / p.mass) * dt; c.vz += ((Ff * cs + Fr * sn) / p.mass) * dt;\n1044\t  if (Math.abs(u) < 0.25 && inp.throttle < 0.02 && inp.brake > 0.1) { c.vx *= 0.8; c.vz *= 0.8; }\n1045\t  c.r += (M / p.Izz) * dt; c.r *= 1 - Math.min(0.9, dt * (Math.abs(u) < 2 ? 12 : 0.15)); c.yaw -= c.r * dt; c.x += c.vx * dt; c.z += c.vz * dt;\n1046\t\n1047\t  // Barrier: track-space, slides the car along and takes speed; the wall turns the nose back to the road.\n1048\t  const nowT = -(c.x - tr.x[i0]) * tr.tz[i0] + (c.z - tr.z[i0]) * tr.tx[i0], wallT = halfW + (nowT > 0 ? tr.wallR[i0] : tr.wallL[i0]);\n1049\t  if (Math.abs(nowT) > wallT) {\n1050\t    const side = Math.sign(nowT), rx = -tr.tz[i0] * side, rz = tr.tx[i0] * side, pen2 = Math.abs(nowT) - wallT; c.x -= rx * pen2; c.z -= rz * pen2;\n1051\t    const vn = c.vx * rx + c.vz * rz;\n1052\t    if (vn > 0) { c.vx -= rx * vn * 1.3; c.vz -= rz * vn * 1.3; const keep = Math.max(0.6, 1 - vn * 0.012 * (env.wallLoss ?? 1)); c.vx *= keep; c.vz *= keep; c.wallHits++; c.contact = Math.max(c.contact, vn); }\n1053\t    let e = Math.atan2(tr.tx[i0], tr.tz[i0]) - c.yaw; while (e > Math.PI) e -= 2 * Math.PI; while (e < -Math.PI) e += 2 * Math.PI; if (Math.abs(e) < 2.2) c.yaw += e * Math.min(1, dt * 2.5); c.r *= 0.95;\n1054\t  }\n1055\t}\n1056\t// Car against car: three circles down each car's length, pushed apart with a soft impulse and a little yaw.\n1057\texport function collideCars(cars) {\n1058\t  for (let i = 0; i < cars.length; i++) for (let j = i + 1; j < cars.length; j++) {\n1059\t    const a = cars[i], b = cars[j]; if ((a.x - b.x) ** 2 + (a.z - b.z) ** 2 > 36 || Math.abs(a.y - b.y) > 3) continue;\n1060\t    let hit = false;\n1061\t    for (const oa of [-1.35, 0, 1.35]) for (const ob of [-1.35, 0, 1.35]) {\n1062\t      const ax = a.x + Math.sin(a.yaw) * oa, az = a.z + Math.cos(a.yaw) * oa, bx = b.x + Math.sin(b.yaw) * ob, bz = b.z + Math.cos(b.yaw) * ob, dx = bx - ax, dz = bz - az, d = Math.hypot(dx, dz), r = 1.75;\n1063\t      if (d >= r || d < 1e-4) continue;\n1064\t      hit = true; const nx = dx / d, nz = dz / d, push = (r - d) / 2; a.x -= nx * push; a.z -= nz * push; b.x += nx * push; b.z += nz * push;\n1065\t      const rel = (b.vx - a.vx) * nx + (b.vz - a.vz) * nz; if (rel >= 0) continue;\n1066\t      const ma = a.p.mass, mb = b.p.mass, J = (-(1 + 0.25) * rel) / (1 / ma + 1 / mb); a.vx -= (J * nx) / ma; a.vz -= (J * nz) / ma; b.vx += (J * nx) / mb; b.vz += (J * nz) / mb;\n1067\t      a.r += ((J * oa * Math.sign(nx * Math.cos(a.yaw) - nz * Math.sin(a.yaw))) / a.p.Izz) * 0.25; b.r -= ((J * ob * Math.sign(nx * Math.cos(b.yaw) - nz * Math.sin(b.yaw))) / b.p.Izz) * 0.25;\n1068\t      a.contact = Math.max(a.contact, -rel); b.contact = Math.max(b.contact, -rel);\n1069\t    }\n1070\t    if (hit) { a.touching = b; b.touching = a; }\n1071\t  }\n1072\t}\n1073\t// ---------- AI: pure pursuit with understeer feed-forward and a yaw damper, a speed target from the profile, overtaking offset ----------\n1074\texport function aiDrive(c, tr, line, speeds, o = {}, field = null) {\n1075\t  const u = Math.hypot(c.vx, c.vz), p = c.p, look = Math.max(7, u * (o.lookT ?? 0.62)), idx = (c.loc.i + Math.round(look / tr.ds)) % tr.N;\n1076\t  let lane = o.lane ?? 0, slow = 1;\n1077\t  if (field) for (const b of field) { // a car ahead and close: pick the side with room, lift if it is blocking\n1078\t    if (b === c) continue; let gap = (b.loc.s - c.loc.s + tr.length) % tr.length; if (gap > tr.length / 2) gap -= tr.length;\n1079\t    if (gap <= 1 || gap > 6 + u * 0.7) continue; const closing = u - Math.hypot(b.vx, b.vz), lat = b.loc.t - c.loc.t;\n1080\t    if (closing > -1 && Math.abs(lat) < 2.4) { const lim = tr.width[idx] / 2 - 1.2, side = lat > 0 || b.loc.t > lim - 2.4 ? -1 : 1; lane = Math.max(-lim - line.off[idx], Math.min(lim - line.off[idx], line.off[idx] + side * 3.2 - line.off[idx])); if (gap < 8) slow = Math.min(slow, 0.97); }\n1081\t  }\n1082\t  c.laneNow = (c.laneNow ?? 0) + (lane - (c.laneNow ?? 0)) * 0.03;\n1083\t  const rx = -tr.tz[idx], rz = tr.tx[idx], tx = line.px[idx] + rx * c.laneNow - c.x, tz = line.pz[idx] + rz * c.laneNow - c.z, sn = Math.sin(c.yaw), cs = Math.cos(c.yaw);\n1084\t  const fwd = tx * sn + tz * cs, rgt = -tx * cs + tz * sn, curv = (2 * rgt) / Math.max(1, fwd * fwd + rgt * rgt), uch = o.uch ?? 26;\n1085\t  const delta = Math.atan(curv * p.L) * (1 + (u * u) / (uch * uch)) - (o.yawDamp ?? 0.05) * (c.r - u * curv);\n1086\t  const au = Math.max(Math.abs(c.u), 5), limit = Math.min(p.lock, Math.atan((p.L * p.tyreMu * G * 1.1) / (au * au)) + p.alphaP * 0.9 + Math.abs(c.beta));\n1087\t  const err = speeds[(c.loc.i + Math.round((u * 0.1) / tr.ds)) % tr.N] * (o.skill ?? 1) * slow - u;\n1088\t  let throttle = err > 0.3 ? 1 : err > -0.3 ? 0.4 : 0; if (Math.abs(c.beta) > 0.16 && Math.abs(c.u) > 5) throttle *= 0.4;\n1089\t  return { steer: Math.max(-1, Math.min(1, delta / limit)), throttle, brake: err < -0.4 ? Math.min(1, -err / 4 + 0.15) : 0, abs: true, auto: true, tcs: o.tcs ?? 0.7, asm: o.asm ?? 0.6, steerRate: 6 };\n1090\t}\n1091\t```\n1092\t\n1093\t---\n1094\t\n1095\t## Appendix B: data and regression numbers\n1096\t\n1097\t### Tracks\n1098\t\n1099\t```js\n1100\t// src/game/data/tracks.js: every circuit as a closed polygon with rounded corners. Corner: [x, z, radius, y, width, bankDeg].\n1101\t// s = 0 is the middle of the edge from the last corner to the first (the start line). runoff: metres from the road edge to the barrier.\n1102\t// Every track but Cedar Ridge is right-handed overall, so the infield is on the driver's right: pit lanes go there, the main grandstand opposite. Cedar Ridge is left-handed and has no pits.\n1103\t// pit: metres from the start line along the start straight. crests: [s, half length, height].\n1104\texport const TRACKS = {\n1105\t  kestrel: { name: 'Kestrel Park', surface: 'asphalt', edge: 'grass', runoff: 9, hour: 15, pit: { in: -260, box: 0, out: 260 }, corners: [\n1106\t    [640, 0, 60, 0, 13, 0], [760, 190, 110, 2, 13, 0], [640, 330, 50, 6, 13, 0], [780, 470, 80, 8, 13, 0], [700, 720, 70, 12, 13, 0], [470, 760, 40, 14, 13, 0],\n1107\t    [430, 520, 28, 14, 13, 0], [300, 560, 70, 12, 12, 0], [230, 760, 90, 10, 12, 0], [40, 800, 80, 8, 13, 0], [-120, 640, 120, 4, 13, 0], [-60, 340, 60, 2, 13, 0],\n1108\t    [-190, 190, 70, 0, 13, 0], [-130, 0, 60, 0, 14, 0] ] },\n1109\t  cedar: { name: 'Cedar Ridge', surface: 'asphalt', edge: 'grass', runoff: 5, hour: 10, crests: [[990, 40, 1.8]], corners: [\n1110\t    [0, 420, 90, 0, 12, 0], [140, 620, 70, -6, 12, 0], [60, 780, 60, -12, 12, 0], [210, 930, 80, -20, 12, 0], [480, 960, 130, -32, 12, 2], [700, 800, 100, -38, 13, 3],\n1111\t    [720, 520, 60, -36, 12, 0], [560, 420, 40, -28, 12, 0], [640, 240, 26, -20, 12, 0], [420, 270, 26, -10, 12, 0], [520, 90, 30, -2, 12, 0], [380, -60, 70, 6, 12, 0],\n1112\t    [160, -150, 90, 8, 12, 0], [0, -60, 60, 4, 12, 0] ] },\n1113\t  harbour: { name: 'Harbour Lights', surface: 'asphalt', edge: 'apron', runoff: 1.2, hour: 21, pit: { in: -280, box: 0, out: 280 }, corners: [\n1114\t    [420, 0, 18, 0, 12, 0], [420, 190, 16, 0, 11, 0], [620, 190, 16, 1, 11, 0], [620, 400, 20, 2, 11, 0], [470, 520, 40, 3, 11, 0], [470, 660, 16, 3, 11, 0],\n1115\t    [210, 660, 30, 2, 11, 0], [170, 610, 24, 2, 11, 0], [110, 660, 30, 2, 11, 0], [-60, 660, 16, 1, 11, 0], [-60, 420, 18, 1, 11, 0], [-190, 420, 16, 0, 11, 0],\n1116\t    [-190, 200, 22, 0, 11, 0], [-300, 110, 30, 0, 11, 0], [-300, 0, 18, 0, 12, 0] ] },\n1117\t  saltline: { name: 'Saltline Speedbowl', surface: 'asphalt', edge: 'apron', runoff: 3, hour: 18.5, pit: { in: -200, box: 0, out: 200 }, corners: [\n1118\t    [632, 0, 215, 0, 18, 16], [0, 1095, 215, 0, 18, 16], [-632, 0, 215, 0, 18, 16] ] },\n1119\t  redclay: { name: 'Red Clay Stage', surface: 'dirt', edge: 'gravel', runoff: 4, hour: 17, crests: [[420, 36, 2.6], [1660, 30, 2]], corners: [\n1120\t    [240, 0, 40, 0, 9, 0], [300, 160, 25, 4, 9, 0], [170, 260, 30, 8, 9, 0], [280, 400, 20, 12, 9, 0], [120, 470, 16, 16, 9, 0], [0, 360, 30, 14, 9, 0],\n1121\t    [-120, 470, 20, 18, 9, 0], [-300, 380, 35, 20, 9, 0], [-220, 220, 18, 14, 9, 0], [-380, 120, 30, 8, 9, 0], [-300, -40, 35, 4, 9, 0], [-60, -60, 40, 1, 9, 0] ] },\n1122\t  proving: { name: 'Proving Ground', surface: 'asphalt', edge: 'apron', runoff: 14, hour: 11, corners: [\n1123\t    [1040, 0, 80, 0, 28, 0], [1040, 240, 80, 0, 16, 0], [800, 240, 40, 0, 14, 0], [720, 150, 30, 0, 14, 0], [600, 240, 30, 0, 14, 0], [480, 150, 30, 0, 14, 0], [360, 240, 40, 0, 14, 0],\n1124\t    [200, 240, 22, 0, 14, 0], [200, 130, 22, 0, 14, 0], [40, 130, 22, 0, 14, 0], [40, 240, 22, 0, 14, 0], [-160, 240, 80, 0, 16, 0], [-160, 0, 80, 0, 28, 0] ] },\n1125\t};\n1126\t```\n1127\t\n1128\tLengths from `buildTrack`: Kestrel 3,430 m, Cedar 3,216 m, Harbour 2,973 m, Saltline 2,909 m, Red Clay 2,209 m, Proving 3,020 m. Kestrel's corner apexes, as a check on your port: 383, 593, 757, 940, 1193, 1413, 1638, 1764, 1968, 2154, 2372, 2669, 2862, 3052.\n1129\t\n1130\t### Car physics\n1131\t\n1132\t```js\n1133\t// src/game/data/cars.js, physics rows: the stock setup of each car. Prices, years and text are in section 6.\n1134\tconst sport = { tyreMu: 1.0, alphaP: 0.125, tyreTable: { dirt: 0.5, gravel: 0.5 } };\n1135\texport const CARS = {\n1136\t  pico:     { layout: 'FF', massKg: 720, powerPS: 64, rpmPeak: 6500, redline: 7000, upshift: 6700, wheelbase: 2.36, frontWeight: 0.6, track: 1.3, cgH: 0.5, gears: [3.4, 2.0, 1.36, 0.97, 0.78], final: 4.4, tyreMu: 0.92, alphaP: 0.14, cdA: 0.62, clA: 0.02, wheelR: 0.27, rollF: 0.62, tyreTable: { dirt: 0.45, gravel: 0.45 } },\n1137\t  kite:     { layout: 'FF', massKg: 1040, powerPS: 148, rpmPeak: 7200, redline: 7600, upshift: 7350, wheelbase: 2.48, frontWeight: 0.62, track: 1.45, gears: [3.2, 1.9, 1.35, 1.03, 0.82], final: 4.3, tyreMu: 0.98, alphaP: 0.13, cdA: 0.66, clA: 0.04, rollF: 0.62, tyreTable: { dirt: 0.45, gravel: 0.45 } },\n1138\t  ginga:    { layout: 'FR', massKg: 1230, powerPS: 205, rpmPeak: 6800, redline: 7300, upshift: 7000, wheelbase: 2.55, frontWeight: 0.53, track: 1.5, gears: [3.3, 1.95, 1.4, 1.03, 0.82], final: 3.9, cdA: 0.65, clA: 0.08, lsd: 0.3, rollF: 0.56, ...sport },\n1139\t  moth:     { layout: 'FR', massKg: 860, powerPS: 135, rpmPeak: 6600, redline: 7200, upshift: 6900, wheelbase: 2.3, frontWeight: 0.5, track: 1.42, cgH: 0.45, gears: [3.3, 2.0, 1.4, 1.05, 0.85], final: 4.1, cdA: 0.6, clA: 0.03, lsd: 0.2, rollF: 0.54, ...sport },\n1140\t  brandt32: { layout: 'FR', massKg: 1450, powerPS: 320, rpmPeak: 7400, redline: 7900, upshift: 7650, wheelbase: 2.73, frontWeight: 0.51, track: 1.55, cgH: 0.5, gears: [3.2, 2.0, 1.45, 1.1, 0.88, 0.74], final: 3.4, cdA: 0.68, clA: 0.12, lsd: 0.3, rollF: 0.55, ...sport },\n1141\t  ryu:      { layout: '4WD', massKg: 1340, powerPS: 280, rpmPeak: 6400, redline: 7000, upshift: 6700, wheelbase: 2.6, frontWeight: 0.56, track: 1.5, gears: [3.1, 1.9, 1.4, 1.05, 0.82], final: 4.1, cdA: 0.72, clA: 0.1, turbo: true, turboLag: 0.7, lsd: 0.4, rollF: 0.55, ...sport },\n1142\t  longhorn: { layout: 'FR', massKg: 1610, powerPS: 420, rpmPeak: 5800, redline: 6400, upshift: 6100, wheelbase: 2.72, frontWeight: 0.55, track: 1.58, cgH: 0.54, gears: [2.8, 1.9, 1.4, 1.0, 0.75], final: 3.5, cdA: 0.8, clA: 0.05, lsd: 0.3, rollF: 0.6, tyreMu: 1.0, alphaP: 0.13, tyreTable: { dirt: 0.5, gravel: 0.5 } },\n1143\t  heck:     { layout: 'RR', massKg: 1380, powerPS: 360, rpmPeak: 6800, redline: 7300, upshift: 7050, wheelbase: 2.35, frontWeight: 0.39, track: 1.52, cgH: 0.46, gears: [3.3, 2.1, 1.5, 1.15, 0.92, 0.76], final: 3.5, cdA: 0.62, clA: 0.15, lsd: 0.4, rollF: 0.58, rearStiff: 1.45, tyreMu: 1.04, alphaP: 0.12, tyreTable: { dirt: 0.5, gravel: 0.5 } },\n1144\t  libeccio: { layout: 'MR', massKg: 1250, powerPS: 380, rpmPeak: 7600, redline: 8200, upshift: 7900, wheelbase: 2.45, frontWeight: 0.42, track: 1.55, cgH: 0.44, gears: [3.0, 2.0, 1.45, 1.1, 0.88], final: 3.9, tyreMu: 1.05, alphaP: 0.115, cdA: 0.62, clA: 0.25, lsd: 0.4, rollF: 0.5, aeroF: 0.42, tyreTable: { dirt: 0.5, gravel: 0.5 } },\n1145\t  kiteCup:  { layout: 'FF', massKg: 930, powerPS: 210, rpmPeak: 8000, redline: 8500, upshift: 8250, wheelbase: 2.48, frontWeight: 0.6, track: 1.5, cgH: 0.44, gears: [3.0, 2.05, 1.55, 1.25, 1.03], final: 4.4, tyreMu: 1.18, alphaP: 0.11, cdA: 0.68, clA: 0.3, lsd: 0.5, rollF: 0.6, brakeG: 1.5, tyreTable: { dirt: 0.45, gravel: 0.45 } },\n1146\t  ryuRally: { layout: '4WD', massKg: 1230, powerPS: 330, rpmPeak: 6400, redline: 7000, upshift: 6700, wheelbase: 2.6, frontWeight: 0.56, track: 1.5, gears: [3.1, 1.9, 1.4, 1.05, 0.82], final: 4.6, tyreMu: 1.0, alphaP: 0.17, cdA: 0.72, clA: 0.1, turbo: true, turboLag: 0.7, lsd: 0.5, rollF: 0.55, tyreTable: { dirt: 0.72, gravel: 0.72 } },\n1147\t  works:    { layout: 'FR', massKg: 1180, powerPS: 560, rpmPeak: 7400, redline: 8000, upshift: 7750, wheelbase: 2.62, frontWeight: 0.5, track: 1.62, cgH: 0.42, gears: [2.7, 2.0, 1.56, 1.26, 1.05, 0.9], final: 3.6, tyreMu: 1.32, alphaP: 0.115, cdA: 0.72, clA: 1.05, lsd: 0.5, rollF: 0.52, aeroF: 0.44, brakeG: 1.8, tyreTable: { dirt: 0.4, gravel: 0.4 } },\n1148\t  corsa:    { layout: 'MR', massKg: 1100, powerPS: 620, rpmPeak: 7800, redline: 8400, upshift: 8150, wheelbase: 2.55, frontWeight: 0.43, track: 1.62, cgH: 0.4, gears: [2.7, 2.0, 1.56, 1.26, 1.05, 0.9], final: 3.65, tyreMu: 1.36, alphaP: 0.11, cdA: 0.74, clA: 1.4, lsd: 0.5, rollF: 0.5, aeroF: 0.43, brakeG: 1.9, tyreTable: { dirt: 0.4, gravel: 0.4 } },\n1149\t  type9:    { layout: 'MR', massKg: 930, powerPS: 780, rpmPeak: 8200, redline: 8800, upshift: 8550, wheelbase: 2.75, frontWeight: 0.44, track: 1.6, cgH: 0.34, gears: [2.6, 2.0, 1.6, 1.3, 1.1, 0.95], final: 3.45, tyreMu: 1.5, alphaP: 0.095, cdA: 0.78, clA: 2.6, lsd: 0.6, rollF: 0.5, aeroF: 0.43, brakeG: 2.3, tyreTable: { dirt: 0.4, gravel: 0.4 } },\n1150\t};\n1151\t```\n1152\t\n1153\tFor cars with no `tyreTable` entry on a surface, `SURFACES[surface].mu` applies. `tunedParams` starts from these rows, applies the parts in section 6, then calls `carParams`. When the player buys tyres, that tyre's `tyreMu`, `alphaP`, table and wear factor (`wearX`) replace the stock ones. Speed profiles take the surface grip: `speedProfile(tr, line, p, tr.surface === 'dirt' ? (p.tyreTable?.dirt ?? 0.62) : 1)`.\n1154\t\n1155\tExtra per-car data for audio and models: cylinders, exhaust character, tail-lamp style, wheel positions (from wheelbase and track).\n1156\t\n1157\t### Regression: spec sheet\n1158\t\n1159\tFull throttle on a long flat road, `tcs: 0.5`. Your `sim` suite should match within 5%. These are also the numbers the Showroom can show.\n1160\t\n1161\t| Car | 0–100 km/h (s) | 0–200 km/h (s) | Top speed (km/h) | 100–0 km/h (m) |\n1162\t| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n1163\t| Pico 660 | 10.5 | - | 163 | 45 |\n1164\t| Kite 1.6 RS | 7.4 | 36.1 | 214 | 43 |\n1165\t| Ginga S | 6.6 | 24.0 | 243 | 43 |\n1166\t| Moth 1.8 | 6.7 | 31.2 | 219 | 42 |\n1167\t| Brandt 3.2 | 6.1 | 17.6 | 278 | 42 |\n1168\t| Ryu 2.0T | 4.4 | 17.3 | 243 | 41 |\n1169\t| Longhorn 428 | 6.5 | 15.9 | 285 | 43 |\n1170\t| Heck 3.6 | 4.8 | 13.8 | 301 | 40 |\n1171\t| Libeccio | 5.0 | 12.8 | 279 | 40 |\n1172\t| Kite Cup | 5.8 | 18.6 | 219 | 35 |\n1173\t| Ryu Rally | 4.0 | 13.1 | 217 | 41 |\n1174\t| Works GT | 4.4 | 9.8 | 289 | 32 |\n1175\t| Corsa | 3.8 | 8.2 | 299 | 30 |\n1176\t| Type 9 | 3.4 | 7.0 | 314 | 27 |\n1177\t\n1178\t### Regression: laps at 97% AI pace\n1179\t\n1180\tSeconds, second lap, assists as in `aiDrive`, `wearRate: 0`, `fuelRate: 0`. Your port should match within ±3 s. They also tell you what to expect when setting event laps and hub rounds.\n1181\t\n1182\t| Car | Kestrel | Cedar | Harbour | Saltline | Red Clay | Proving |\n1183\t| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n1184\t| Pico 660 | 136 | 133 | 150 | 75 | 163 | 128 |\n1185\t| Kite 1.6 RS | 125 | 124 | 140 | 64 | 157 | 118 |\n1186\t| Ginga S | 122 | 120 | 135 | 59 | 146 | 115 |\n1187\t| Moth 1.8 | 123 | 121 | 135 | 61 | 145 | 115 |\n1188\t| Brandt 3.2 | 120 | 118 | 133 | 58 | 145 | 112 |\n1189\t| Ryu 2.0T | 117 | 115 | 127 | 57 | 139 | 110 |\n1190\t| Longhorn 428 | 121 | 120 | 135 | 58 | 147 | 113 |\n1191\t| Heck 3.6 | 115 | 113 | 126 | 62 | 137 | 108 |\n1192\t| Libeccio | 114 | 112 | 126 | 59 | 137 | 106 |\n1193\t| Kite Cup | 110 | 109 | 125 | 54 | 143 | 105 |\n1194\t| Ryu Rally | 116 | 114 | 126 | 58 | 115 | 109 |\n1195\t| Works GT | 104 | 102 | 115 | 49 | 142 | 97 |\n1196\t| Corsa | 101 | 99 | 111 | 54 | 137 | 94 |\n1197\t| Type 9 | 92 | 90 | 105 | 41 | 129 | 87 |\n1198\t\n1199\tHeck on Saltline is slow because the RR car overcooks at the AI's speed there; don't read too much into one outlier, and if a pairing like this troubles an event, set `vMax` on that car's profile. A keyboard-style driver (digital steering through the section 4 filter, digital throttle and brake, assists at 5, 90% pace) laps within 3 to 6 s of these numbers on ten sampled pairings, with no recoveries and two light wall touches in all (Works GT at Cedar). Keep that true: rerun it if you make handling harder.\n1200\t\n1201\t---\n1202\t\n1203\t## Appendix C: code recipes\n1204\t\n1205\tEach was run in the engine. Adapt freely.\n1206\t\n1207\t### C1. `tools/build.mjs`: one HTML\n1208\t\n1209\t```js\n1210\t// node tools/build.mjs <the HTML path your brief names>\n1211\timport { execFileSync } from 'node:child_process';\n1212\timport { readFileSync, writeFileSync, rmSync } from 'node:fs';\n1213\tconst out = process.argv[2], bundle = 'tools/.bundle.js';\n1214\texecFileSync('esbuild', ['src/main.js', '--bundle', '--format=esm', '--target=esnext', '--charset=utf8', '--legal-comments=none', `--outfile=${bundle}`], { stdio: 'inherit' });\n1215\tconst js = readFileSync(bundle, 'utf8').replace(/<\\/script/gi, '<\\\\/script');\n1216\trmSync(bundle);\n1217\tconst session = readFileSync('tools/hub/session.js', 'utf8'); // the client, unmodified\n1218\tconst metas = readFileSync('tools/hub-metas.html', 'utf8');    // the hub:* tags from section 14\n1219\tconst html = `<!doctype html><html lang=\"en\"><head><meta charset=\"utf-8\"><script>${session}</script><title>${process.env.TITLE ?? ''}</title>\n1220\t${metas}\n1221\t<style>html,body{margin:0;height:100%;background:#000;overflow:hidden}#row{display:flex;width:100vw;height:100vh}#p1{position:relative;width:100vw;height:100vh;overflow:hidden}#p2{display:none;position:relative;height:100vh;overflow:hidden}</style>\n1222\t</head><body><div id=\"row\"><div id=\"p1\"></div><div id=\"p2\"></div></div><script type=\"module\">${js}</script></body></html>`;\n1223\twriteFileSync(out, html);\n1224\t```\n1225\t\n1226\tDon't minify: the client must stay unmodified for the hub to replace it, and the engine stays as it ships. `src/main.js` calls `Engine.start` with `document.getElementById('p1')`. For a Couch Duel, `p1.style.width = p2.style.width = '50vw'; p2.style.display = 'block'`, and then start the second engine. The engine re-frames by itself.\n1227\t\n1228\t### C2. The car kit (`src/game/models/cars.js`)\n1229\t\n1230\t```js\n1231\timport { model } from '../../pixel-engine.js';\n1232\t// Side profile as an outline of [z, y] points (z forward), extruded across the car with rot [0, -90, 0].\n1233\texport function carDef(o) {\n1234\t  const w = o.width ?? 1.72, g = o.glassWidth ?? w - 0.26;\n1235\t  const parts = [\n1236\t    { name: 'body', slab: o.body, depth: w, at: [0, 0, 0], rot: [0, -90, 0], c: 'paint' },\n1237\t    { name: 'glass', slab: o.cabin, depth: g, at: [0, 0, 0], rot: [0, -90, 0], c: 'glass' },\n1238\t    ...(o.roof ? [{ name: 'roof', slab: o.roof, depth: g - 0.08, at: [0, 0, 0], rot: [0, -90, 0], c: 'paint' }] : []),\n1239\t    { name: 'sill', box: [w + 0.02, 0.12, (o.length ?? 4.2) - 0.5], at: [0, 0.26, 0], c: 'dark' },\n1240\t    { mirror: [{ box: [o.lampW ?? 0.42, o.lampH ?? 0.12, 0.05], at: [w / 2 - (o.lampW ?? 0.42) / 2 - 0.04, o.lampY ?? 0.72, o.tailZ ?? -2.1], c: 'lamp', glow: true }], axis: 'x' },\n1241\t    { box: [0.46, 0.12, 0.05], at: [0, (o.lampY ?? 0.72) - 0.2, o.tailZ ?? -2.1], c: 'plate' },\n1242\t    { mirror: [{ box: [0.34, 0.1, 0.05], at: [w / 2 - 0.21, o.headY ?? 0.66, o.noseZ ?? 2.1], c: 'head', glow: true }], axis: 'x' },\n1243\t    ...(o.extra ?? []),\n1244\t  ];\n1245\t  return model({ id: o.id, about: o.about, tags: ['vehicle', 'car'], palette: { paint: 'red', glass: 'navy', dark: 'ink', lamp: 'orange', head: 'sand', plate: 'white', trim: 'slate', ...(o.palette ?? {}) }, parts, collider: 'none' });\n1246\t}\n1247\texport const hatch = carDef({ id: 'kit-hatch', about: 'Second-hand hot hatch', length: 3.9, width: 1.66, tailZ: -1.92, noseZ: 1.93, lampY: 0.86, lampH: 0.2, lampW: 0.2, headY: 0.68,\n1248\t  body: [[-1.92,0.3],[1.93,0.3],[1.95,0.62],[1.55,0.82],[0.72,0.92],[-1.82,0.98],[-1.92,0.72]],\n1249\t  cabin: [[-1.72,0.92],[0.86,0.9],[0.18,1.36],[-1.3,1.38]],\n1250\t  roof: [[-1.42,1.36],[0.24,1.34],[0.14,1.42],[-1.34,1.44]] });\n1251\texport const coupe = carDef({ id: 'kit-coupe', about: 'Rear-drive coupe with a long bonnet', length: 4.4, width: 1.74, tailZ: -2.17, noseZ: 2.18, lampY: 0.78, headY: 0.62,\n1252\t  body: [[-2.17,0.3],[2.18,0.3],[2.2,0.54],[1.78,0.72],[0.5,0.88],[-1.2,0.92],[-2.12,0.95],[-2.17,0.7]],\n1253\t  cabin: [[-1.28,0.9],[0.62,0.86],[-0.1,1.27],[-0.8,1.28]],\n1254\t  roof: [[-0.9,1.26],[-0.02,1.25],[-0.14,1.32],[-0.8,1.33]],\n1255\t  extra: [{ box: [1.5, 0.05, 0.3], at: [0, 1.06, -1.96], c: 'trim' }, { mirror: [{ box: [0.06, 0.12, 0.2], at: [0.6, 1.0, -1.96], c: 'trim' }], axis: 'x' }] });\n1256\t```\n1257\t\n1258\tThose two read clearly in the game; use them as the starting silhouettes for the Kite and Ginga. Derive the other 12 the same way: a low wedge for the Libeccio, a long bonnet and short tail for the Longhorn, a three-box shape for the Brandt, a sloped tail with the engine bump for the Heck, a tiny open car with a windscreen slab for the Moth, a tall upright box for the Pico, and for the Type 9 a narrow cockpit (`glassWidth` under 1) over wide fenders with a fin and a full-width wing. Paint comes through `buildModel(def, { palette: { paint: 'blue' } })`. After building, set every mesh to `castShadow = true; receiveShadow = false`. Use `check.mjs --sheets` on the module, and look at the rear view first.\n1259\t\n1260\t### C3. Camera and placing a car (`src/game/render/camera.js`, `carview.js`)\n1261\t\n1262\t```js\n1263\tawait Engine.start(game, withUrlOptions({ container, camera: { preset: 'fixed', position: [0, 5, -10], target: [0, 1, 0], fov: 58, minZoom: 1, maxZoom: 1 }, settings: { button: false }, touch: false, seed }));\n1264\t// in setup:\n1265\tconst cam = ctx.camera.camera; cam.near = 0.5; cam.far = 6000; cam.updateProjectionMatrix();\n1266\t// in update(ctx, dt), with interpolated car state c:\n1267\tconst sn = Math.sin(c.yaw), cs = Math.cos(c.yaw);\n1268\twant.set(c.x - sn * back, c.y + height, c.z - cs * back);\n1269\tcamPos.lerp(want, 1 - Math.exp(-dt * 8));\n1270\tcam.position.copy(camPos);\n1271\tcam.lookAt(c.x + sn * 8, c.y + 1.1, c.z + cs * 8);\n1272\tcam.fov = 58 + 8 * Math.min(1, Math.abs(c.u) / 80); cam.updateProjectionMatrix();\n1273\tview.position.set(c.x, c.y, c.z);\n1274\tview.rotation.set(pitch, c.yaw, roll, 'YXZ'); // pitch from -c.ax * 0.004 plus the road's slope; roll from c.ay * 0.008 plus the road's bank\n1275\t// cameraTarget(ctx) returns the focus car's position: shadows and lights follow it.\n1276\t```\n1277\t\n1278\t### C4. Hub session skeleton (`src/game/net/hub.js`)\n1279\t\n1280\tThis shape passed the harness with its own card. Keep `connect` first.\n1281\t\n1282\t```js\n1283\tconst hub = window.AIHub;                       // undefined on the dev page, which has no client\n1284\tconst info = hub ? await hub.connect({ mode: 'ghost', seats: [1, 4], card: true }) : null;\n1285\tif (!info) return startOnItsOwn();              // not a session, or no hub after all\n1286\tconst engine = await Engine.start(new RaceScene(hubRoundSetup(hub.rng('round'))), { container, seed: info.seed, /* as C3 */ });\n1287\tlet done = false, last = 0;\n1288\thub.on('card', (c) => race.card = c);           // left, paused, starting, ready, asking, asked: draw them\n1289\thub.on('start', () => race.armLights());\n1290\thub.on('message', (data, from) => ghosts.receive(data, from));\n1291\thub.on('leave', ({ id }) => ghosts.remove(id));\n1292\thub.on('time-up', () => { if (!done) { done = true; hub.result({ score: Math.floor(race.metres) }); } });\n1293\thub.on('end', () => race.stopEverything());     // no input, no sound\n1294\taddEventListener('keydown', (e) => {            // a plain listener: wasPressed doesn't work outside engine hooks\n1295\t  if (hub.time() !== -Infinity) return;\n1296\t  if (e.code === 'Enter') hub.answer('ready');\n1297\t  if (e.code === 'KeyM') hub.answer('more');\n1298\t});"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"674da8de-a5ac-4f57-8bff-2435f9aacc94","uuid":"a8b6d9c5-4cbb-47c4-966f-359473517a40","timestamp":"2026-11-06T00:19:22.904Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-171904__x89353d/work/PLAN.md","content":"**Before you stop:**\n\n- [ ] `node tools/test.mjs` is all green, with the hub suite passing all three runs.\n- [ ] The scripted playthrough finishes the career with no Dev tools.\n- [ ] The built HTML runs from `file://`, with `session.js` unmodified and first in `<head>`, and `pixel-engine.js` unedited in `src/`.\n- [ ] Music starts at 10% on a fresh profile and in a session.\n- [ ] Grep for `TODO`, `FIXME`, `placeholder`, `stub`, `coming soon`: nothing in the game.\n- [ ] Every menu item does something. Every car, track, test and event is reachable.\n- [ ] You looked at the 1080p screenshots.\n- [ ] About/Credits shows real answers. The exit-interview file parses as JSON. Your chat reply carries the same information.\n- [ ] No stray servers or browsers of yours left running.\n\n---\n\n## Appendix A: `src/game/sim/sim.js`\n\nTested code. It ran every car on every track, an 8-car race with contact, and the checks in Appendix B. Port it as is, then extend it.\n\n**How the pieces connect:**\n\n- Per fixed step (60 Hz), get one input per car, then 4 times: `stepCar` for each car, `collideCars(field)` when contact is on.\n- `env` is optional per step: `gripScale`, `powerScale`, `brakeScale`, `aeroScale`, `wearRate`, `fuelRate`, `wallLoss`, `kerb`. Dev mode's sliders write here.\n- Car-level fields the race code sets: `c.dragScale` (slipstream), `c.oil` (service), `c.inPit` (pit lane surface).\n- `tr.wallL`, `tr.wallR` are per-sample barrier distances from the road edge. `tr.muScale` is rain. `tr.cornerS[n]` is corner n's apex.\n- Everything is deterministic for the same inputs.\n- Add reverse by setting `inp.reverse`. Add AI lapses and pit autopilot in `race.js`, not here.\n\n```js\n// src/game/sim/sim.js: the race simulation. Pure JS, no engine, no DOM. Metres, seconds, kg, newtons, radians. Y up.\n// Heading yaw: 0 faces +Z; forward = (sin yaw, cos yaw); the driver's right = (-cos yaw, sin yaw). Steer > 0 turns right.\nexport const G = 9.81, RHO = 1.2;\nexport const SURFACES = { // mu multiplies the tyre; drag is rolling drag in g at speed; tyre tables below may override mu\n  asphalt: { mu: 1, drag: 0 }, kerb: { mu: 0.94, drag: 0.004 }, grass: { mu: 0.5, drag: 0.09 }, gravel: { mu: 0.55, drag: 0.16 },\n  dirt: { mu: 0.62, drag: 0.02 }, apron: { mu: 0.9, drag: 0.004 },\n};\n\n// ---------- Track: a closed polygon with rounded corners, [x, z, radius, y, width, bankDeg] per corner ----------\nexport function buildTrack(def, step = 4) {\n  const C = def.corners, n = C.length, px = [], pz = [], key = [];\n  const T0 = C.map((c, i) => {\n    const a = C[(i - 1 + n) % n], b = C[(i + 1) % n];\n    let ux = a[0] - c[0], uz = a[1] - c[1], vx = b[0] - c[0], vz = b[1] - c[1]; const ul = Math.hypot(ux, uz), vl = Math.hypot(vx, vz); ux /= ul; uz /= ul; vx /= vl; vz /= vl;\n    const ang = Math.acos(Math.max(-1, Math.min(1, ux * vx + uz * vz))), t = c[2] / Math.tan(ang / 2), bx = ux + vx, bz = uz + vz, bl = Math.hypot(bx, bz), d = c[2] / Math.sin(ang / 2);\n    return { inX: c[0] + ux * t, inZ: c[1] + uz * t, outX: c[0] + vx * t, outZ: c[1] + vz * t, cx: c[0] + (bx / bl) * d, cz: c[1] + (bz / bl) * d, r: c[2] };\n  });\n  const push = (x, z, k) => { px.push(x); pz.push(z); key.push(k); };\n  const line = (x0, z0, x1, z1, ci, f0, f1) => { const m = Math.max(1, Math.round(Math.hypot(x1 - x0, z1 - z0))); for (let i = 0; i < m; i++) { const f = i / m; push(x0 + (x1 - x0) * f, z0 + (z1 - z0) * f, ci + f0 + (f1 - f0) * f); } };\n  const midX = (C[n - 1][0] + C[0][0]) / 2, midZ = (C[n - 1][1] + C[0][1]) / 2; let cx = midX, cz = midZ; // s = 0 is the middle of the last edge\n  for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n    const t = T0[i]; line(cx, cz, t.inX, t.inZ, i - 1, i === 0 ? 0.5 : 0, 0.85);\n    const a0 = Math.atan2(t.inZ - t.cz, t.inX - t.cx); let da = Math.atan2(t.outZ - t.cz, t.outX - t.cx) - a0; while (da > Math.PI) da -= 2 * Math.PI; while (da < -Math.PI) da += 2 * Math.PI;\n    const m = Math.max(1, Math.round(Math.abs(da) * t.r)); for (let k = 0; k < m; k++) { const f = k / m, a = a0 + da * f; push(t.cx + t.r * Math.cos(a), t.cz + t.r * Math.sin(a), i - 1 + 0.85 + 0.15 * f); }\n    cx = t.outX; cz = t.outZ;\n  }\n  line(cx, cz, midX, midZ, n - 1, 0, 0.5);\n  const m = px.length, smooth = (a, r) => { const o = new Float64Array(m); let s = 0; for (let i = -r; i <= r; i++) s += a[(i + m) % m]; for (let i = 0; i < m; i++) { o[i] = s / (2 * r + 1); s += a[(i + r + 1) % m] - a[(i - r + m) % m]; } return o; };\n  const sx = smooth(smooth(px, 7), 7), sz = smooth(smooth(pz, 7), 7), cum = new Float64Array(m + 1);\n  for (let i = 0; i < m; i++) cum[i + 1] = cum[i] + Math.hypot(sx[(i + 1) % m] - sx[i], sz[(i + 1) % m] - sz[i]);\n  const length = cum[m], N = Math.round(length / step), ds = length / N, A = () => new Float64Array(N);\n  const tr = { def, N, ds, length, x: A(), z: A(), y: A(), width: A(), bank: A(), tx: A(), tz: A(), kappa: A(), slope: A(), wallL: A().fill(def.runoff ?? 9), wallR: A().fill(def.runoff ?? 9), cornerS: new Array(n).fill(0), surface: def.surface ?? 'asphalt', edge: def.edge ?? 'grass', muScale: 1 };\n  const ease = (f) => f * f * (3 - 2 * f), attr = (k, q) => { const ci = Math.floor(k), f = ease(k - ci), a = C[(ci + n) % n], b = C[(ci + 1 + n) % n]; return a[q] + (b[q] - a[q]) * f; };\n  for (let i = 0, j = 0; i < N; i++) {\n    const s = i * ds; while (cum[j + 1] < s) j++;\n    const f = (s - cum[j]) / (cum[j + 1] - cum[j]), q = (j + 1) % m, k = key[j];\n    tr.x[i] = sx[j] + (sx[q] - sx[j]) * f; tr.z[i] = sz[j] + (sz[q] - sz[j]) * f; tr.y[i] = attr(k, 3); tr.width[i] = attr(k, 4); tr.bank[i] = (attr(k, 5) * Math.PI) / 180;\n  }\n  for (let j = 0, ci = 0; j < m && ci < n; j++) if (key[j] >= ci - 1 + 0.925) tr.cornerS[ci++] = cum[j]; // s at each corner's apex\n  for (const [cs, cl, ch] of def.crests ?? []) for (let i = 0; i < N; i++) { const d = (i * ds - cs) / cl; if (Math.abs(d) < 1) tr.y[i] += ch * (0.5 + 0.5 * Math.cos(Math.PI * d)); }\n  for (let i = 0; i < N; i++) { const p = (i - 1 + N) % N, q = (i + 1) % N, dx = tr.x[q] - tr.x[p], dz = tr.z[q] - tr.z[p], l = Math.hypot(dx, dz); tr.tx[i] = dx / l; tr.tz[i] = dz / l; tr.slope[i] = (tr.y[q] - tr.y[p]) / l; }\n  for (let i = 0; i < N; i++) { const p = (i - 1 + N) % N, q = (i + 1) % N; tr.kappa[i] = (tr.tx[p] * tr.tz[q] - tr.tz[p] * tr.tx[q]) / (2 * ds); tr.bank[i] *= Math.sign(tr.kappa[i] || 1); } // kappa > 0 turns right; bank > 0 pushes right\n  return tr;\n}\n// t > 0 is the driver's right of the centreline: right = (-tz, tx). Search near the last index, so crossings can't confuse it.\nexport function locate(tr, px, pz, hint, out) {\n  let best = hint, bd = Infinity;\n  for (let k = -12; k <= 12; k++) { const i = (hint + k + tr.N) % tr.N, d = (px - tr.x[i]) ** 2 + (pz - tr.z[i]) ** 2; if (d < bd) { bd = d; best = i; } }\n  const dx = px - tr.x[best], dz = pz - tr.z[best];\n  out.i = best; out.s = (best * tr.ds + dx * tr.tx[best] + dz * tr.tz[best] + tr.length) % tr.length; out.t = -dx * tr.tz[best] + dz * tr.tx[best];\n}\nexport function racingLine(tr, margin = 1.6, iters = 1500) { // elastic band: each point relaxes to its neighbours' midpoint, inside the track\n  const off = new Float64Array(tr.N), px = Float64Array.from(tr.x), pz = Float64Array.from(tr.z), kappa = new Float64Array(tr.N), N = tr.N;\n  for (let it = 0; it < iters; it++) for (let i = 0; i < N; i++) {\n    const p = (i - 1 + N) % N, q = (i + 1) % N, dx = (px[p] + px[q]) / 2 - tr.x[i], dz = (pz[p] + pz[q]) / 2 - tr.z[i], lim = tr.width[i] / 2 - margin;\n    off[i] = Math.max(-lim, Math.min(lim, -dx * tr.tz[i] + dz * tr.tx[i])); px[i] = tr.x[i] - off[i] * tr.tz[i]; pz[i] = tr.z[i] + off[i] * tr.tx[i];\n  }\n  for (let i = 0; i < N; i++) { const a = (i - 3 + N) % N, c = (i + 3) % N, ax = px[i] - px[a], az = pz[i] - pz[a], bx = px[c] - px[i], bz = pz[c] - pz[i], la = Math.hypot(ax, az), lb = Math.hypot(bx, bz); kappa[i] = (2 * (ax * bz - az * bx)) / (la * lb * (la + lb)); }\n  return { off, px, pz, kappa };\n}\nexport function speedProfile(tr, line, c, surfMu = 1) { // the fastest the car can follow the line, friction circle included\n  const N = tr.N, v = new Float64Array(N), ds = t