MaterialOptions\n\n- `map?: Texture | null`: Base color texture. Switched to nearest filtering (crisp texels, no mip blur).\n- `vertexColors?: boolean`: Multiply by the geometry's `color` attribute (vertex colors).\n- `rim?: number`: A hard-banded rim light in this colour (hex) on grazing, upward-facing surfaces: a silhouette that reads against dark floors (monsters in dark levels). Added to the emissive, so `material.emissive` (hit flashes) still work\n- `dissolve?: boolean`: Pixel dissolve: the material reads its own `dissolve` property (0 = solid, 1 = gone) and discards a per-art-pixel noise pattern below it, with a 1-pixel glowing front in the rim colour (or white). Set it on per-body \n\n## 5. Physics\n\n### interface BoxOptions\n\n- `position: [number, number, number]`\n- `halfExtents: [number, number, number]`\n- `rotationY?: number`\n- `friction?: number`\n- `density?: number`\n5073:### interface WaterOptions\n5074-\n5075-- `size: readonly [number, number]`: Width (x) and depth (z) of the surface, m.\n5076-- `at: readonly [number, number, number]`: Centre of the surface at rest.\n5077-- `segments?: readonly [number, number]`: Grid quads along x and z (default: one per ripple cell, or 4 per metre without ripples).\n5078-- `waves?: readonly Wave[]`\n5079-- `ripples?: RippleField | null`: A ripple field covering the same rectangle (its size and centre must match).\n5080-- `deep?: number`: Colours (hex): troughs, crests, foam.\n5081-- `shallow?: number`\n5082-- `foam?: number`\n5083-- `foamAt?: number`: Height above rest (m) where foam starts. Default: 75% of the waves' combined height (the tallest crests).\n5084-- `opacity?: number`: 1: opaque; less: see-through by a 4×4 ordered dither per art pixel.\n5085-\n5086-### class WaterSurface\n5087-\n5088-- `new WaterSurface(o: WaterOptions)`\n5089-- `readonly size: readonly [number, number]`\n5090-- `waves: Wave[]`\n5091-- `readonly ripples: RippleField | null`\n11:5. Physics: `BoxOptions`, `Breakable`, `BreakableOptions`, `Breakables`, `BridgeOptions`, `Built`, `chain`, `ChainOptions`, `CharacterAnim`, `CharacterController`, `CharacterOptions`, `Chunk`, `clothGrid`, `ClothOptions`, `Crumble`, `CrumbleOptions`, `DoorOptions`, `DriveInput`, `explode`, `ExplosionOptions`, `Field`, `fieldAcceleration`, `FieldOptions`, `FIXED_DT`, `FloaterOptions`, `Floaters`, `ForceFields`, `fractureBox`, `FractureOptions`, `hingeDoor`, `InstancedBodies`, `InstancedBodiesOptions`, `InstancedShape`, `KinematicBody`, `Mover`, `MoverOptions`, `moverRotation`, `Movers`, `orbit`, `pathPoint`, `pendulum`, `Physics`, `PhysicsState`, `Ragdoll`, `RagdollOptions`, `RagdollPart`, `Rewind`, `RewindOptions`, `RippleField`, `RippleOptions`, `ropeBridge`, `ropeLine`, `seeded`, `seesaw`, `SeesawOptions`, `softBlob`, `springPad`, `SpringPadOptions`, `Trigger`, `TriggerOptions`, `TriggerShape`, `Vehicle`, `VehicleOptions`, `VerletBody`, `VerletOptions`, `waterHeight`, `WaterWave`, `WAVES_CALM`, `WAVES_CHOPPY`\n2116:### WAVES_CALM\n2119:const WAVES_CALM: readonly Wave[]\n2124:### WAVES_CHOPPY\n2127:const WAVES_CHOPPY: readonly Wave[]\n4741:### interface SkyState\n4742-\n4743-- `readonly sunDir: [number, number, number]`: Unit vector toward the sun (or the moon, at night).\n4744-- `readonly sunColor: number`\n4745-- `readonly sunIntensity: number`\n4746-- `readonly ambientColor: number`\n4747-- `readonly ambientIntensity: number`\n4748-- `readonly sky: number`: Background (sky) and fog colour.\n4749-- `readonly night: number`: 0 by day, 1 deep at night: lanterns, stars, windows.\n4750-\n4751-### interface Snapshot\n4752-\n4753-- `readonly format: 1`\n4754-- `readonly engine: string`: The engine version that took it (a different one may not restore the same).\n4755-- `readonly game: string`: The game's name: a snapshot restores into the same game.\n3952:### interface BoidOptions\n3953-\n3954-- `bounds?: { min: Vec3; max: Vec3 }`: Agents stay inside this box (they steer back in near its walls).\n3955-- `view?: number`: Neighbour radius (m). Default 2.\n3956-- `space?: number`: Desired gap (m): closer neighbours push apart. Default 0.8.\n3957-- `maxSpeed?: number`\n3958-- `minSpeed?: number`\n3959-- `maxForce?: number`: Steering acceleration limit (m/s²).\n3960-- `separation?: number`: Rule weights.\n3961-- `alignment?: number`\n3962-- `cohesion?: number`\n3963-- `flat?: boolean`: Keep to a horizontal plane (fish in a pond, sheep on a field): y never changes.\n3964-- `margin?: number`: How far inside the bounds the push back in starts (m). Default the view radius; small for a tight pen.\n3965-- `seed?: number`\n3966-\n### interface LightRequestOptions\n\n- `position?: Vector3 | readonly [number, number, number]`: World position (copied). Ignored while `follow` is set (then it is `follow` + `offset`).\n- `follow?: Object3D | null`: Follow an object's world position every frame (a projectile, a monster, the hero).\n- `offset?: readonly [number, number, number]`: Offset from `follow` (world axes).\n- `color?: ColorRepresentation`\n- `intensity?: number`: Point light intensity at full strength (before flicker and fades). Default 4.\n- `radius?: number`: Reach in metres (PointLight.distance: light is 0 beyond it). Default 6.\n- `decay?: number`: Distance falloff exponent (PointLight.decay; a uniform, free to change). Default 1.2.\n- `flicker?: FlickerPreset`\n- `priority?: number`: Importance multiplier: the hero's light 4, a loot beam 2, a torch 1 (default).\n- `fadeIn?: number`: Fade times in seconds (defaults 0.25 in, 0.2 out).\n- `fadeOut?: number`\n- `lifetime?: number`: Release automatically after this many seconds (spell flashes, explosions).\n- `name?: string`: Optional label for debugging (`pool.describe()`).\n\n### interface MergeOptions\n\n- `castShadow?: boolean`: Override castShadow on every merged mesh (default: keep each source mesh's flag).\n- `receiveShadow?: boolean`: Override receiveShadow on every merged mesh (default: keep each source mesh's flag).\n\n4598:### interface PrecipitationOptions\n4599-\n4600-- `kind: PrecipitationKind`\n4601-- `count: number`: Most drops at once (the instance count).\n4602-- `area?: readonly [number, number, number]`: Width, height and depth of the air the drops fall through, around the centre.\n4603-- `color?: number`: Drop colour (hex).\n4604-- `speed?: number`: Fall speed (m/s). Rain 16, snow 1.4.\n4605-\n4606-### interface Recording\n4607-\n4608-- `readonly format: 1`\n2703:### interface ParticlePreset\n2704-\n2705-A particle effect as data. Sizes are in art pixels (whole pixels, so particles stay crisp\n2706-squares), colors are palette names stepped over each particle's life (no blending).\n2707-\n2708-- `count: Range`: Particles per burst.\n2709-- `life: Range`: Seconds each particle lives.\n2710-- `speed: Range`: Launch speed, world units / s.\n2711-- `direction?: Vec3`: Main launch direction (default straight up).\n2712-- `spread?: number`: Cone half-angle around `direction`, degrees (180 = every direction). Default 180.\n2713-- `flatten?: number`: Multiply vertical launch speed (0.2 = dust that hugs the ground). Default 1.\n2714-- `gravity?: number`: Downward acceleration, world units / s² (negative floats up). Default 0.\n2715-- `drag?: number`: Velocity damping per second (0 = none).\n2716-- `size: readonly [number, number]`: Size in art pixels at birth and at death (rounded to whole pixels).\n2717-- `colors: readonly PaletteColor[]`: Palette colors stepped through over the lifetime.\n2718-- `radius?: number`: Random spawn offset radius, world units.\n2719-- `max?: number`: Pool size (max alive at once). Default 256.\n2720-\n2721-### type ParticlePresetName\n2722-\n2723-```ts\n2724-type ParticlePresetName = keyof typeof PARTICLES\n2725-```\n2670:### interface BurstOptions\n2671-\n2672-- `count?: number`: Override the particle count.\n2673-- `direction?: Vec3`: Override the launch direction (e.g. opposite to a skid).\n2674-- `speed?: number`: Multiply launch speed.\n2675-- `scale?: number`: Multiply size.\n2676-- `colors?: readonly PaletteColor[]`: Override the colors for this burst.\n2677-\n2678-### class ParticlePool\n2679-\n2680-Fixed-size particle storage with CPU simulation. Alive particles are packed at the\n2884:### buildModel()\n2885-\n2886-```ts\n2887-function buildModel(idOrDef: string | ModelDef, opts: ModelOptions = {}): ModelBuild\n2888-```\n2889-\n2890-### class Catalog\n--\n3077:### MODEL_LIBRARY\n3078-\n3079-```ts\n3080-const MODEL_LIBRARY: ModelCatalog\n3081-```\n3082-\n3083-The engine's built-in models (src/engine/model/library/<family>.ts). Games add their own\n114:| `lamp-post` | 0.68 × 2.1 × 0.3 |  | iron night, flame sand | lighting, town | Iron street lamp with a hanging lantern |\n132:| `pine` | 2.01 × 3.88 × 2.01 | h 4 (3–5) | bark plum, leaf teal, leaf2 green | nature, tree | Conifer: a plum trunk under four stacked cones, teal and green in turn; `h` is its height |\n133:| `oak` | 2.72 × 3.77 × 2.28 | h 4 (3–5) | bark red, leaf green, leaf2 lime | nature, tree | Round broadleaf tree: a red trunk on roots under a crown of 3-5 lumps, green round the sides and lime o\n140:| `birch` | 2.2 × 4.49 × 1.76 | h 4.5 (3–6) | bark white, mark ink, leaf lime, leaf2 green | nature, tree | Birch: a slender white trunk barred with ink marks under a light, open crown of small lu\n143:| `cactus` | 0.8 × 2.47 × 1.34 | h 2.4 (1.2–3.5) | body green, arm teal, arm2 lime, rib lime, bud red | nature, plant, desert | Saguaro cactus: a green column striped with lime ribs, 2-3 arms elbo\n147:| `boulders` | 1.35 × 0.84 × 1.41 | size 1.2 (0.6–2) | stone slate, stone2 mist, stone3 night | nature, stone | Pile of 3-5 boulders (seeded): a big slate one with smaller mist and night ones heap\n180:| `haystack` | 1.69 × 1.77 × 1.8 | h 1.6 (1–2.4) | hay sand, hay2 orange, rope red | town, farm, hay | Beehive haystack bound by a rope, darker loose hay round its foot and a straw tuft on its cro","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected