{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FMF2Qq2Y8R3LDmzdSusdwy","type":"tool_result","content":"Build the game PLAN.md describes. Take your file names and what to hand in from TASK.md, which is filled in for you. Keep your progress in PROGRESS.md, so you can pick up where you were after your context is compacted.\n---\n11:Package: For ease of deployment and sharing provide a single html file [GameTitle-SOURCE-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261105-171904].html. Dependencies that can be downloaded do not have to be included in the htm\n23:Working Environment and deliverable:\n24:Create a subfolder called [GameTitle-SOURCE-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261105-171904] to keep all your dev files in. You can develop separate modules, then bundle into a single file [GameTitle-SOURCE-claude-opu\n93:CRITICAL: Put Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback in your chat reply and an in-game About/Credits screen. Write \"unknown\" for anything you can't confirm.\n109:Exit interview: before you finish, also save these answers as exit-interview.json in this folder's root, beside the game's .html: one JSON object in exactly the shape below, every value filled in (\"unknown\"\n---\n2558:### renderSound()\n2561:function renderSound(def: SoundDef, sampleRate = 44100, seed = 1): Float32Array<ArrayBuffer>\n2564:Render a sound to mono samples in -1..1.\n2665:rendered to samples once, then played as a buffer. Deterministic (seeded noise), so\n3444:`texture`: TSL's `texture()` samples a map, and games import both.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"674da8de-a5ac-4f57-8bff-2435f9aacc94","uuid":"1b5b0cdb-5a7a-45bf-8a19-07ab37bd1d70","timestamp":"2026-11-06T03:23:11.446Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"Build the game PLAN.md describes. Take your file names and what to hand in from TASK.md, which is filled in for you. Keep your progress in PROGRESS.md, so you can pick up where you were after your context is compacted