y, mud that wash\n29 | Rally and endurance | One-on-one gap racing on dirt, and a ten-lap night\n30 | Catalogue voice | Sincere, precise, gently dry writing (section 11) |\n34 1. **The corner is the game.** Braking, line and throttle decide everythin\n35 2. **Every car is a character.** If two cars feel the same, fix the data.\n36 3. **The garage is the story.** Progress is a car that is yours and that y\n37 4. **Calm between storms.** Menus breathe. Nothing shouts. Then the green \n49 - No real car makers or models. Use only the fictional marques in section \n50 - No real or source circuits. Use the layouts in Appendix B; they are orig\n51 - Nothing from the source's logo, menu layout, fonts, tagline, event names\n52 - The title is a playful riff on the source's name, as the brief asks. It \n53 - About and credits say \"inspired by\" and name the source, as the brief as\n61 | Question | Result |\n63 | One HTML from `file://`? | Yes. Bundle with esbuild, inline after escapi\n64 | Chase camera? | Use preset `fixed`: its `step()` leaves the camera alone\n65 | Does a racing game read at 480×270? | Very well. A car seen from the cha\n66 | Car models as data? | Yes. Side-profile polygons (`slab`) extruded acros\n67 | Split screen on one TV? | Yes. Two `Engine.start` calls in two side-by-s\n68 | Hub conformance with WebGPU in iframes? | Passes: 2 players; 4 players w\n69 | The engine's `Vehicle`? | An arcade vehicle (default top speed 16 m/s, n\n70 | Is a real car model feasible and stable? | Yes. Appendix A has run every\n71 | `Engine.headless` and `check.mjs --headless`? | Work for a game whose `c\n72 | Pixel ghost cars? | `toonMaterial(color, { dissolve: true })` cloned per\n73 | Rain and night? | `Precipitation`, `applySky(engine, skyAt(hour))` and `\n79 1. **Menus and `loadGame`.** `loadGame` frees the scene's objects, the mus\n80 2. **Pausing.** `engine.paused` and `timeScale = 0` make `dt` 0 and drop q\n81 3. **Volumes.** Engine defaults are master 0.8, sfx 1, musi