r the session and are cleared by Reset. Medals and records earned with\n698 The brief points to the AI Hub session protocol, in the hub repository's `lib/hub/README\n702 Why ghost and not shared world: every copy runs its own physics at 240 Hz with no input \n704 **Tags,** in `<head>`, after the client:\n707 <meta name=\"hub:session\" content=\"1\">\n708 <meta name=\"hub:session-players\" content=\"1-4\">\n709 <meta name=\"hub:session-mode\" content=\"ghost\">\n710 <meta name=\"hub:session-minutes\" content=\"4\">\n711 <meta name=\"hub:session-goal\" content=\"Lowest time wins: same car, same track\">\n712 <meta name=\"hub:session-howto\" content=\"Steer stick or A D. R2 or W go. L2 or S brake.\">\n713 <meta name=\"hub:webgpu\" content=\"required\">\n716 The hub's examples also carry `hub:type` and `hub:players`: use `Game`, and `1-2` for pl\n718 **A round:**\n735 Your brief's phrase \"as well as for the game on its own\" is read two ways, and this plan\n737 **Couch Duel** (Arcade Gate): two players, one TV, split screen, any track and car, with\n739 **Also:** Time Trial's ghost can be raced in turn by whoever holds the pad (\"Pass the pa\n745 The brief says exactly what this must contain. Build it once, as data, then show it two \n750 **The About screen** is paged for the TV, reached from Title, Map and Settings:\n756 Paginate long answers. Never use a dense wall: it's still a TV.\n758 Use the same answers in your final chat reply, as the brief requires. Don't estimate usa\n760 **The `aiHub` block:** type `Game`, genre `Racing`, source and series for the source nam\n762 **Research:** the director's research on the kit, the hub protocol and the source is fol\n768 The brief's rules: one command that prints only failures and a one-line count; rerun onl\n770 Write `node tools/test.mjs [suite...]`. Suites cache by file hash, so an unchanged suite\n783 **Machine notes.**\n791 **Look at these at 1920×1080**, when their code changes, because no script can judge the\n797 Ri