{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HyRk1fgBhwphsGXXyg8K8Y","type":"tool_result","content":"TESTING: Headless and scripted tests allowed; one command printing failures and a count. Ran node tools/test.mjs: sim, data, career, audit (evidence for every line of the plan), headless, play (whole career by bot), browser (Chromium; WebKit only to confirm the no-WebGPU message), audio and hub (harness 2 players, 4 players with latency, host leaving, plus the session menu). Screenshots at 1920x1080 for what scripts cannot judge. No subagents\ntestingFeedback 0 46 by my count: 13 from the scripted suites and the career bot, 3 from page errors in the browser, 13 from looking at screenshots, and 17 from three line-by-line reads of the plan that the tests had missed. No human has driven it, so handling feel is untested beyond scripted drivers: that is a real gap, not a pass.\ntestingFeedback 1 8: AI crash at the first race, menus left over the race, pause closing on the press that opened it, a crash on the hub card, boot broken by one of my own patches, the Red Clay and Featherweight fields that blocked the career, tyres destroyed on the Saltline banking in the Grand Prix, and Options in a hub round opening the pausing menu, which the harness did not catch.\ntestingFeedback 2 The whole-career bot. It played real screens through to the ending, and its log exposed accidental pit entries, unbeatable fields and the banking problem, none of which a unit test would have shown. Close behind it: tools/audit.mjs, which forced evidence for every line of the plan and found what passing tests had hidden.\ntestingFeedback 3 The audio centroid check was the least helpful: its one failure was a mistake in the test's own frequency analysis, and the engine synth was right from the start.\nengineFeedback 0 Engine.headless: the same game code, in Node, without a GPU. It let a bot play the whole career in about three minutes, and the HUD, particles and tweens all just worked there.\nengineFeedback 1 Yes. I assumed a box's width runs along its heading, so long buildings came out sideways until I saw a screenshot. I passed the wrong arguments to analyzeClip by guessing its signature. Screen transitions never resolve while the engine is in manual step mode, which hung one of my scripts.\nengineFeedback 2 The driving: the car model came with the plan, and on it I built the race rules, career, replay director, track mesh and dressing, and the engine synth. For the engine's own part, the menu system with focus, prompts and glyphs was the largest thing I had to build.\nengineFeedback 3 Getting a large world built from one GeoBatch to look right with shadows: acne on walls at grazing angles, and the choice of which surfaces may receive them. Also the HUD's colour argument: a CSS string fails only at paint time, outside the game's hooks, so engine.errors stays empty.\nengineFeedback 4 none\nengineFeedback 5 Have hud.rect and hud.sprite reject bad input (an unknown colour name, an undefined sprite row) at the call, with a message, instead of throwing later in the paint step where the stack says nothing about the game.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"674da8de-a5ac-4f57-8bff-2435f9aacc94","uuid":"fa8fed0f-0518-4c0b-a256-115600f67932","timestamp":"2026-11-06T04:48:59.199Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"TESTING: Headless and scripted tests allowed; one command printing failures and a count. Ran node tools/test.mjs: sim, data, career, audit (evidence for every line of the plan), headless, play (whole career by bot), browser (Chromium; WebKit only to confirm the no-WebGPU message), audio and hub (harness 2 players, 4 players with latency, host leaving, plus the session menu). Screenshots at 1920x1080 for what scripts cannot judge. No subagents\ntestingFeedback 0 46 by my count: 13 from the scripted suites and the career bot, 3 from page errors in the browser, 13 from looking at screenshots, and 17 from three line-by-line reads of the plan that the tests had missed. No human has driven it, so handling feel is untested beyond scripted drivers: that is a real gap, not a pass.\ntestingFeedback 1 8: AI crash at the first race, menus left over the race, pause closing on the press that opened it, a crash on the hub card, boot broken by one of my own patches, the Red Clay and Featherweight fields that blocked the career, tyres destroyed on the Saltline banking in the Grand Prix, and Options in a hub round opening the pausing menu, which the harness did not catch.\ntestingFeedback 2 The whole-career bot. It played real screens through to the ending, and its log exposed accidental pit entries, unbeatable fields and the banking problem, none of which a unit test would have shown. Close behind it: tools/audit.mjs, which forced evidence for every line of the plan and found what passing tests had hidden.\ntestingFeedback 3 The audio centroid check was the least helpful: its one failure was a mistake in the test's own frequency analysis, and the engine synth was right from the start.\nengineFeedback 0 Engine.headless: the same game code, in Node, without a GPU. It let a bot play the whole career in about three minutes, and the HUD, particles and tweens all just worked there.\nengineFeedback 1 Yes. I assumed a box's width runs along its heading, so long buildings came out sideways until I saw a screenshot. I passed the wrong arguments to analyzeClip by guessing its signature. Screen transitions never resolve while the engine is in manual step mode, which hung one of my scripts.\nengineFeedback 2 The driving: the car model came with the plan, and on it I built the race rules, career, replay director, track mesh and dressing, and the engine synth. For the engine's own part, the menu system with focus, prompts and glyphs was the largest thing I had to build.\nengineFeedback 3 Getting a large world built from one GeoBatch to look right with shadows: acne on walls at grazing angles, and the choice of which surfaces may receive them. Also the HUD's colour argument: a CSS string fails only at paint time, outside the game's hooks, so engine.errors stays empty.\nengineFeedback 4 none\nengineFeedback 5 Have hud.rect and hud.sprite reject bad input (an unknown colour name, an undefined sprite row) at the call, with a message, instead of throwing later in the paint step where the stack says nothing about the game.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01HyRk1fgBhwphsGXXyg8K8Y","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
