{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgm53FKkQu6f5k2wcTPZw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Va2xoRW7n2HBAFQQ25Qx1x","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json\np='../exit-interview.json'; d=json.load(open(p))\nd['sourceInformation']['testing']=\"Headless and scripted tests allowed; one command printing failures and a count. Ran node tools/test.mjs: sim, data, career, audit (evidence for every line of the plan), headless, behave (the plan's behaviours done and measured), layout (every screen at 360, 480 and 640 wide), play (whole career by bot), browser (Chromium; WebKit and Firefox only to confirm the no-WebGPU message), hands (real mouse, wheel, pad and a hub round watched from inside), audio and hub (harness 2 players, 4 players with latency, host leaving, plus the session menu). Screenshots at 1920x1080 for what scripts cannot judge. No subagents\"\nt=d['testingFeedback']\nt[0]=\"60 by my count: 13 from the scripted suites and the career bot, 3 from page errors in the browser, 13 from looking at screenshots, 17 from three line-by-line reads of the plan that the tests had missed, and 14 from a last pass of behaviour and layout suites, written because much of my audit only proved that code existed. No human has driven it, so handling feel is untested beyond scripted drivers: that is a real gap, not a pass.\"\nt[1]=\"9: AI crash at the first race, menus left over the race, pause closing on the press that opened it, a crash on the hub card, boot broken by one of my own patches, the Red Clay and Featherweight fields that blocked the career, tyres destroyed on the Saltline banking in the Grand Prix, Options in a hub round opening the pausing menu, which the harness did not catch, and attract mode starting 10 s into any screen opened over the title or Map, which threw a reader back to the Map and could cut into a prize ceremony.\"\nt[2]=\"The whole-career bot. It played real screens through to the ending, and its log exposed accidental pit entries, unbeatable fields and the banking problem, none of which a unit test would have shown. Close behind it: the last behaviour suite, which ran what the audit had only seen in code. With 1652 checks already passing, it found the attract bug and a replay director cutting nearly every frame.\"\ne=d['engineFeedback']\ne[1]=\"Yes. I assumed a box's width runs along its heading, so long buildings came out sideways until I saw a screenshot. I passed the wrong arguments to analyzeClip by guessing its signature. Screen transitions never resolve while the engine is in manual step mode, which hung one of my scripts. Engine.headless runs its own camera rig unless it is given the game's preset, so my first camera checks read the wrong camera.\"\njson.dump(d,open(p,'w'),ensure_ascii=False,indent=2); open(p,'a').write('\\n')\njson.load(open(p)); print('parses')\np='../PROGRESS.md'; s=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace(\"- menu stack stayed over a race (headless suite)\\n\",\"- menu stack stayed over a race (headless suite)\\n- Last pass, suites behave, layout and hands: attract started on any screen opened over the title or Map; replay director cut nearly every frame; hold Triangle took 1.4 s to recover; keyboard steering used the return rate on its first frame; test card brief ran off the screen and its tip was cut mid-word; subtitles covered buttons (test card, licence lists, event card, parts); About overflowed at 360 wide; Map labels, the GP's locked reason, the 200's round card and narrow race messages overflowed; mix kept making engine synths after the hub's end; replay camera swung to the new car before the cut\\n\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\nnode tools/build.mjs | tail -n 1 | cut -c1-30; node tools/audit.mjs 2>&1 | tail -n 1 | cut -c1-110","description":"Update exit interview and progress, rebuild, refresh audit","timeout":60000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3029,"cache_read_input_tokens":469875,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3029},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"674da8de-a5ac-4f57-8bff-2435f9aacc94","uuid":"deb5f7d0-bd89-43e4-9d29-fbe611fd4e95","timestamp":"2026-11-06T04:49:16.006Z","request_id":"req_011Cgm53F38wUqkeehNWoCNP","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01Va2xoRW7n2HBAFQQ25Qx1x":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json\np='../exit-interview.json'; d=json.load(open(p))\nd['sourceInformation']['testing']=\"Headless and scripted tests allowed; one command printing failures and a count. Ran node tools/test.mjs: sim, data, career, audit (evidence for every line of the plan), headless, behave (the plan's behaviours done and measured), layout (every screen at 360, 480 and 640 wide), play (whole career by bot), browser (Chromium; WebKit and Firefox only to confirm the no-WebGPU message), hands (real mouse, wheel, pad and a hub round watched from inside), audio and hub (harness 2 players, 4 players with latency, host leaving, plus the session menu). Screenshots at 1920x1080 for what scripts cannot judge. No subagents\"\nt=d['testingFeedback']\nt[0]=\"60 by my count: 13 from the scripted suites and the career bot, 3 from page errors in the browser, 13 from looking at screenshots, 17 from three line-by-line reads of the plan that the tests had missed, and 14 from a last pass of behaviour and layout suites, written because much of my audit only proved that code existed. No human has driven it, so handling feel is untested beyond scripted drivers: that is a real gap, not a pass.\"\nt[1]=\"9: AI crash at the first race, menus left over the race, pause closing on the press that opened it, a crash on the hub card, boot broken by one of my own patches, the Red Clay and Featherweight fields that blocked the career, tyres destroyed on the Saltline banking in the Grand Prix, Options in a hub round opening the pausing menu, which the harness did not catch, and attract mode starting 10 s into any screen opened over the title or Map, which threw a reader back to the Map and could cut into a prize ceremony.\"\nt[2]=\"The whole-career bot. It played real screens through to the ending, and its log exposed accidental pit entries, unbeatable fields and the banking problem, none of which a unit test would have shown. Close behind it: the last behaviour suite, which ran what the audit had only seen in code. With 1652 checks already passing, it found the attract bug and a replay director cutting nearly every frame.\"\ne=d['engineFeedback']\ne[1]=\"Yes. I assumed a box's width runs along its heading, so long buildings came out sideways until I saw a screenshot. I passed the wrong arguments to analyzeClip by guessing its signature. Screen transitions never resolve while the engine is in manual step mode, which hung one of my scripts. Engine.headless runs its own camera rig unless it is given the game's preset, so my first camera checks read the wrong camera.\"\njson.dump(d,open(p,'w'),ensure_ascii=False,indent=2); open(p,'a').write('\\n')\njson.load(open(p)); print('parses')\np='../PROGRESS.md'; s=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace(\"- menu stack stayed over a race (headless suite)\\n\",\"- menu stack stayed over a race (headless suite)\\n- Last pass, suites behave, layout and hands: attract started on any screen opened over the title or Map; replay director cut nearly every frame; hold Triangle took 1.4 s to recover; keyboard steering used the return rate on its first frame; test card brief ran off the screen and its tip was cut mid-word; subtitles covered buttons (test card, licence lists, event card, parts); About overflowed at 360 wide; Map labels, the GP's locked reason, the 200's round card and narrow race messages overflowed; mix kept making engine synths after the hub's end; replay camera swung to the new car before the cut\\n\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\nnode tools/build.mjs | tail -n 1 | cut -c1-30; node tools/audit.mjs 2>&1 | tail -n 1 | cut -c1-110","description":"Update exit interview and progress, rebuild, refresh audit","timeout":60000}}}
